{
  "@@locale": "en",
  "tagline": "Ten runs across the Drowned Mile. The water remembers.",
  "@tagline": {
    "description": "One line under the campaign's name (NULL TIDE) in the pack list."
  },
  "signals.reminder.0": "Tide table says you have a window. Tide tables have been wrong for eleven years, so I would not spend it sitting down.",
  "@signals.reminder.0": {
    "description": "MARROW. Nudges the runner to go out. A notification sent between runs; never spoken. At most 180 characters."
  },
  "signals.reminder.1": "Nothing is sinking faster than usual. Take the morning if you want it.",
  "@signals.reminder.1": {
    "description": "MARROW. Nudges the runner to go out. A notification sent between runs; never spoken. At most 180 characters."
  },
  "signals.reminder.2": "Water is where it should be, which happens about twice a month. Use it.",
  "@signals.reminder.2": {
    "description": "MARROW. Nudges the runner to go out. A notification sent between runs; never spoken. At most 180 characters."
  },
  "signals.reminder.3": "No work, no crisis, no reason. Go anyway. It helps, apparently.",
  "@signals.reminder.3": {
    "description": "MARROW. Nudges the runner to go out. A notification sent between runs; never spoken. At most 180 characters."
  },
  "signals.reminder.4": "The Mile is passable. I am not promising dry, I am promising passable.",
  "@signals.reminder.4": {
    "description": "MARROW. Nudges the runner to go out. A notification sent between runs; never spoken. At most 180 characters."
  },
  "signals.reminder.5": "Knee is bad, the paper still needs carrying, and you are the one with the legs. Think about it.",
  "@signals.reminder.5": {
    "description": "MARROW. Nudges the runner to go out. A notification sent between runs; never spoken. At most 180 characters."
  },
  "signals.reminder.6": "If you are going out, go now. Everything down here gets worse after lunch.",
  "@signals.reminder.6": {
    "description": "MARROW. Nudges the runner to go out. A notification sent between runs; never spoken. At most 180 characters."
  },
  "signals.reminder.7": "I would walk it myself. I have said that about four things today and meant none of them.",
  "@signals.reminder.7": {
    "description": "MARROW. Nudges the runner to go out. A notification sent between runs; never spoken. At most 180 characters."
  },
  "signals.reminder.8": "The water is low enough to cross today. I am told that is the sort of thing you want to know.",
  "@signals.reminder.8": {
    "description": "WREN. Nudges the runner to go out. A notification sent between runs; never spoken. At most 180 characters."
  },
  "signals.reminder.9": "You have not moved since yesterday. I checked. That is not surveillance, that is concern.",
  "@signals.reminder.9": {
    "description": "WREN. Nudges the runner to go out. A notification sent between runs; never spoken. At most 180 characters."
  },
  "signals.reminder.10": "The pumps are holding. Good a morning as you are going to get for it.",
  "@signals.reminder.10": {
    "description": "LEVEE. Nudges the runner to go out. A notification sent between runs; never spoken. At most 180 characters."
  },
  "signals.reminder.11": "Scheduled reminder. Tidal conditions unremarkable. No excuse identified.",
  "@signals.reminder.11": {
    "description": "SYSTEM. Nudges the runner to go out. A notification sent between runs; never spoken. At most 180 characters."
  },
  "signals.ambient.0": "Pump House Seven apologised again last night. Nine seconds, same as always. Sleep well.",
  "@signals.ambient.0": {
    "description": "WREN. Unprompted chatter from the city. A notification sent between runs; never spoken. At most 180 characters."
  },
  "signals.ambient.1": "Something under the Mile is keeping time. Not well. But keeping it.",
  "@signals.ambient.1": {
    "description": "WREN. Unprompted chatter from the city. A notification sent between runs; never spoken. At most 180 characters."
  },
  "signals.ambient.2": "I counted the lights on the far bank. There is one more than last week. Nobody will tell me whose.",
  "@signals.ambient.2": {
    "description": "WREN. Unprompted chatter from the city. A notification sent between runs; never spoken. At most 180 characters."
  },
  "signals.ambient.3": "The gulls have moved inland. The gulls are usually right about this sort of thing.",
  "@signals.ambient.3": {
    "description": "WREN. Unprompted chatter from the city. A notification sent between runs; never spoken. At most 180 characters."
  },
  "signals.ambient.4": "Water came up two centimetres on the Mile this week. Nobody measured it but me.",
  "@signals.ambient.4": {
    "description": "LEVEE. Unprompted chatter from the city. A notification sent between runs; never spoken. At most 180 characters."
  },
  "signals.ambient.5": "Someone has been repainting the depth markers lower. I have repainted them back.",
  "@signals.ambient.5": {
    "description": "LEVEE. Unprompted chatter from the city. A notification sent between runs; never spoken. At most 180 characters."
  },
  "signals.ambient.6": "The east sluice is singing again. It does that when the pressure is wrong.",
  "@signals.ambient.6": {
    "description": "LEVEE. Unprompted chatter from the city. A notification sent between runs; never spoken. At most 180 characters."
  },
  "signals.ambient.7": "Found a chair on the roof of a flooded house. Someone sat up there a long time.",
  "@signals.ambient.7": {
    "description": "LEVEE. Unprompted chatter from the city. A notification sent between runs; never spoken. At most 180 characters."
  },
  "signals.ambient.8": "Salvage board is thin. Everything worth taking is under four metres of water and someone else's name.",
  "@signals.ambient.8": {
    "description": "MARROW. Unprompted chatter from the city. A notification sent between runs; never spoken. At most 180 characters."
  },
  "signals.ambient.9": "A man tried to sell me a door today. A door. Down here.",
  "@signals.ambient.9": {
    "description": "MARROW. Unprompted chatter from the city. A notification sent between runs; never spoken. At most 180 characters."
  },
  "signals.ambient.10": "Insurance assessor came out to the Mile. Took one photograph, left, has not been seen since.",
  "@signals.ambient.10": {
    "description": "WREN. Unprompted chatter from the city. A notification sent between runs; never spoken. At most 180 characters."
  },
  "signals.ambient.11": "The tide brought back a shoe I threw out in spring. I am choosing not to think about it.",
  "@signals.ambient.11": {
    "description": "MARROW. Unprompted chatter from the city. A notification sent between runs; never spoken. At most 180 characters."
  },
  "signals.ambient.12": "Quiet on the water. Quiet is not the same as safe, but it is nicer.",
  "@signals.ambient.12": {
    "description": "MARROW. Unprompted chatter from the city. A notification sent between runs; never spoken. At most 180 characters."
  },
  "signals.ambient.13": "Eleven years today since the districts went under. Nobody is marking it. That is its own kind of marking.",
  "@signals.ambient.13": {
    "description": "MARROW. Unprompted chatter from the city. A notification sent between runs; never spoken. At most 180 characters."
  },
  "signals.ambient.14": "Somebody has been leaving flowers at the sea wall. Same spot, every week, no name.",
  "@signals.ambient.14": {
    "description": "MARROW. Unprompted chatter from the city. A notification sent between runs; never spoken. At most 180 characters."
  },
  "signals.ambient.15": "The ferry is running again. It is not a ferry, it is a man with a boat, but it is running.",
  "@signals.ambient.15": {
    "description": "MARROW. Unprompted chatter from the city. A notification sent between runs; never spoken. At most 180 characters."
  },
  "signals.ambient.16": "Half the Mile lost power for an hour and nobody noticed until the pumps changed note.",
  "@signals.ambient.16": {
    "description": "MARROW. Unprompted chatter from the city. A notification sent between runs; never spoken. At most 180 characters."
  },
  "signals.ambient.17": "Harbour Authority notice. Pedestrian activity logged in a restricted tidal zone. No enforcement action is scheduled. Records are retained.",
  "@signals.ambient.17": {
    "description": "DREDGE. Unprompted chatter from the city. A notification sent between runs; never spoken. At most 180 characters."
  },
  "signals.ambient.18": "Harbour Authority notice. The managed retreat is complete. Reports of residency south of the wall remain unsubstantiated.",
  "@signals.ambient.18": {
    "description": "DREDGE. Unprompted chatter from the city. A notification sent between runs; never spoken. At most 180 characters."
  },
  "signals.ambient.19": "Tidal advisory: high water at dawn. Tidal advisories have been indicative at best since the flood.",
  "@signals.ambient.19": {
    "description": "SYSTEM. Unprompted chatter from the city. A notification sent between runs; never spoken. At most 180 characters."
  },
  "signals.ambient.20": "Structural notice: the Drowned Mile remains condemned. Population of the Drowned Mile: unchanged.",
  "@signals.ambient.20": {
    "description": "SYSTEM. Unprompted chatter from the city. A notification sent between runs; never spoken. At most 180 characters."
  },
  "signals.ambient.21": "Pump network nominal. Seven of nine stations reporting. This is considered nominal.",
  "@signals.ambient.21": {
    "description": "SYSTEM. Unprompted chatter from the city. A notification sent between runs; never spoken. At most 180 characters."
  },
  "signals.debrief.met.0": "Week's accounts, and they balance.",
  "@signals.debrief.met.0": {
    "description": "MARROW. The weekly target was met. Opens the weekly debrief notification; the app appends the week's figures after it. Say nothing specific about the numbers. At most 90 characters."
  },
  "signals.debrief.met.1": "Okay so you actually did the thing and I logged all of it, obviously.",
  "@signals.debrief.met.1": {
    "description": "WREN. The weekly target was met. Opens the weekly debrief notification; the app appends the week's figures after it. Say nothing specific about the numbers. At most 90 characters."
  },
  "signals.debrief.met.2": "The week closes. I have been counting.",
  "@signals.debrief.met.2": {
    "description": "LEVEE. The weekly target was met. Opens the weekly debrief notification; the app appends the week's figures after it. Say nothing specific about the numbers. At most 90 characters."
  },
  "signals.debrief.missed.0": "Tide is nearly out on the week.",
  "@signals.debrief.missed.0": {
    "description": "MARROW. The weekly target was missed. Opens the weekly debrief notification; the app appends the week's figures after it. Say nothing specific about the numbers. At most 90 characters."
  },
  "signals.debrief.missed.1": "Short, and I would rather tell you now than on Monday.",
  "@signals.debrief.missed.1": {
    "description": "MARROW. The weekly target was missed. Opens the weekly debrief notification; the app appends the week's figures after it. Say nothing specific about the numbers. At most 90 characters."
  },
  "signals.debrief.missed.2": "The week is closing and the number is not where it should be.",
  "@signals.debrief.missed.2": {
    "description": "LEVEE. The weekly target was missed. Opens the weekly debrief notification; the app appends the week's figures after it. Say nothing specific about the numbers. At most 90 characters."
  },
  "signals.debrief.idle.0": "Nothing from you this week. Not judging. Counting.",
  "@signals.debrief.idle.0": {
    "description": "MARROW. No runs at all this week. Opens the weekly debrief notification; the app appends the week's figures after it. Say nothing specific about the numbers. At most 90 characters."
  },
  "signals.debrief.idle.1": "You went quiet. I checked twice. Then I checked again.",
  "@signals.debrief.idle.1": {
    "description": "WREN. No runs at all this week. Opens the weekly debrief notification; the app appends the week's figures after it. Say nothing specific about the numbers. At most 90 characters."
  },
  "signals.debrief.idle.2": "No movement recorded this week. The water moved. It always does.",
  "@signals.debrief.idle.2": {
    "description": "LEVEE. No runs at all this week. Opens the weekly debrief notification; the app appends the week's figures after it. Say nothing specific about the numbers. At most 90 characters."
  },
  "nt01.title": "Low Water on the Drowned Mile",
  "@nt01.title": {
    "description": "The title of operation LOW WATER (nt01), shown under its codename."
  },
  "nt01.objective": "Carry a paper tide-chart across the Mile before the water comes back.",
  "@nt01.objective": {
    "description": "One line: what the runner does in operation LOW WATER (nt01)."
  },
  "nt01.brief": "The southern districts went under eleven years ago and the city called it a managed retreat. The people who stayed call it the Drowned Mile. Twice a day the sea pulls back and the old streets show for a few hours, chalk marks and all.\n\nMarrow brokers salvage off the Mile. He needs a chart carried across it while the ground is still ground. Paper, because paper doesn't ping.",
  "@nt01.brief": {
    "description": "The briefing of operation LOW WATER (nt01), read before the run."
  },
  "nt01.debrief": "The chart made it dry. Marrow paid without counting, which Wren later tells you he never does. The water came back forty minutes after you crossed and covered everything you ran on.",
  "@nt01.debrief": {
    "description": "Shown after operation LOW WATER (nt01) is completed."
  },
  "nt01.codex.cdx_drowned_mile.title": "The Drowned Mile",
  "@nt01.codex.cdx_drowned_mile.title": {
    "description": "The title of a codex entry found in operation LOW WATER (nt01). Keep it as it is if it is a name."
  },
  "category.PLACES": "PLACES",
  "@category.PLACES": {
    "description": "A section heading in the codex, set in capitals. Short: one or two words."
  },
  "nt01.codex.cdx_drowned_mile.body": "Eleven years ago the harbour came over the southern dry line and stayed. The city filed it as a managed retreat and moved the maps. The people who stayed built upward — stilts, rooftops, walkways strung between the second floors — and named the place after what it was: a mile of streets that only exist at low water.",
  "@nt01.codex.cdx_drowned_mile.body": {
    "description": "A codex entry about \"The Drowned Mile\", read at leisure."
  },
  "nt01.codex.cdx_tide_routes.title": "Tide Routes",
  "@nt01.codex.cdx_tide_routes.title": {
    "description": "The title of a codex entry found in operation LOW WATER (nt01). Keep it as it is if it is a name."
  },
  "category.STREET": "STREET",
  "@category.STREET": {
    "description": "A section heading in the codex, set in capitals. Short: one or two words."
  },
  "nt01.codex.cdx_tide_routes.body": "Chalk marks on the walls at knee height. White means the ground under it is dry at low water; blue means it looks dry and isn't. The first marks were made by children the summer after the flood, on a dare. The dare stuck, and now the marks are the only map of the Mile that has never been wrong.",
  "@nt01.codex.cdx_tide_routes.body": {
    "description": "A codex entry about \"Tide Routes\", read at leisure."
  },
  "nt01.nt01_b0.headline": "CHANNEL OPEN",
  "@nt01.nt01_b0.headline": {
    "description": "A banner flashed on the run screen in operation LOW WATER (nt01), scene nt01_b0. Capitals, two or three words."
  },
  "nt01.nt01_b0.0": "You're the courier. The one who walked out of Vantar with a heartbeat in a box. Don't answer, the channel's thin.",
  "@nt01.nt01_b0.0": {
    "description": "MARROW, in operation LOW WATER (nt01), scene nt01_b0. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt01.nt01_b0.1": "I'm Marrow. I broker salvage off the Drowned Mile, and I need a piece of paper carried across it before the sea comes home.",
  "@nt01.nt01_b0.1": {
    "description": "MARROW, in operation LOW WATER (nt01), scene nt01_b0. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt01.nt01_b0.2": "Low water in fifty minutes. After that the streets you're about to run on are a harbour. Move.",
  "@nt01.nt01_b0.2": {
    "description": "MARROW, in operation LOW WATER (nt01), scene nt01_b0. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt01.nt01_b1.0": "You're past the stilt market. Everything on your left used to be a bus depot. Everything on your right still is, technically.",
  "@nt01.nt01_b1.0": {
    "description": "MARROW, in operation LOW WATER (nt01), scene nt01_b1. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt01.nt01_b1.1": "The city calls this a managed retreat. Nobody who lives here has ever seen it managed.",
  "@nt01.nt01_b1.1": {
    "description": "MARROW, in operation LOW WATER (nt01), scene nt01_b1. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt01.nt01_b2.headline": "CHART HANDOFF",
  "@nt01.nt01_b2.headline": {
    "description": "A banner flashed on the run screen in operation LOW WATER (nt01), scene nt01_b2. Capitals, two or three words."
  },
  "nt01.nt01_b2.0": "Item received. Paper. Mass negligible. Ink, salt-stable.",
  "@nt01.nt01_b2.0": {
    "description": "SYSTEM, in operation LOW WATER (nt01), scene nt01_b2. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt01.nt01_b2.1": "That's a tide-chart. Hand-drawn. It shows where the ground goes when the water comes, and it exists on nothing with a battery.",
  "@nt01.nt01_b2.1": {
    "description": "MARROW, in operation LOW WATER (nt01), scene nt01_b2. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt01.nt01_b2.2": "Fold it once. Never twice. Go.",
  "@nt01.nt01_b2.2": {
    "description": "MARROW, in operation LOW WATER (nt01), scene nt01_b2. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt01.nt01_b3.0": "You're on a tide route now. Chalk marks on the walls, knee height. White means dry at low water. Blue means it lies.",
  "@nt01.nt01_b3.0": {
    "description": "MARROW, in operation LOW WATER (nt01), scene nt01_b3. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt01.nt01_b3.1": "The marks are older than the flood's official name. Kids made them the first summer, on a dare. The dare stuck.",
  "@nt01.nt01_b3.1": {
    "description": "MARROW, in operation LOW WATER (nt01), scene nt01_b3. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt01.nt01_b4.headline": "SKIFF ON THE WATER",
  "@nt01.nt01_b4.headline": {
    "description": "A banner flashed on the run screen in operation LOW WATER (nt01), scene nt01_b4. Capitals, two or three words."
  },
  "nt01.nt01_b4.0": "Engine noise east. Harbour Authority skiff, running the channel that used to be Fourth Street.",
  "@nt01.nt01_b4.0": {
    "description": "MARROW, in operation LOW WATER (nt01), scene nt01_b4. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt01.nt01_b4.1": "They don't like paper. Paper's the one thing they can't subpoena from a server. Get off the open ground.",
  "@nt01.nt01_b4.1": {
    "description": "MARROW, in operation LOW WATER (nt01), scene nt01_b4. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt01.nt01_b4.escaped.0": "They've turned for the channel. Skiffs can't follow onto ground that's still ground. That's the whole trick of this place.",
  "@nt01.nt01_b4.escaped.0": {
    "description": "MARROW, in operation LOW WATER (nt01), scene nt01_b4, after the runner escapes HARBOUR SKIFF. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt01.nt01_b4.escaped.1": "Good. You run like someone who's been chased by better.",
  "@nt01.nt01_b4.escaped.1": {
    "description": "MARROW, in operation LOW WATER (nt01), scene nt01_b4, after the runner escapes HARBOUR SKIFF. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt01.nt01_b4.caught.0": "Harbour Authority notice. Pedestrian logged in a restricted tidal zone. Identity pending.",
  "@nt01.nt01_b4.caught.0": {
    "description": "DREDGE, in operation LOW WATER (nt01), scene nt01_b4, after HARBOUR SKIFF catches the runner. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt01.nt01_b4.caught.1": "They've got your gait. Not your face. Keep it that way.",
  "@nt01.nt01_b4.caught.1": {
    "description": "MARROW, in operation LOW WATER (nt01), scene nt01_b4, after HARBOUR SKIFF catches the runner. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt01.nt01_b5.0": "Halfway. The water's already coming back behind you. You won't see it, you'll hear it. It sounds like applause.",
  "@nt01.nt01_b5.0": {
    "description": "MARROW, in operation LOW WATER (nt01), scene nt01_b5. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt01.nt01_b5.1": "Don't turn round. People turn round and then they're still turned round when it reaches them.",
  "@nt01.nt01_b5.1": {
    "description": "MARROW, in operation LOW WATER (nt01), scene nt01_b5. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt01.nt01_b6.headline": "PUMP HOUSE",
  "@nt01.nt01_b6.headline": {
    "description": "A banner flashed on the run screen in operation LOW WATER (nt01), scene nt01_b6. Capitals, two or three words."
  },
  "nt01.nt01_b6.0": "Pump House Seven on your left. It's been running since before the flood. Nobody's inside. Nobody's ever inside.",
  "@nt01.nt01_b6.0": {
    "description": "MARROW, in operation LOW WATER (nt01), scene nt01_b6. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt01.nt01_b6.1": "Sometimes at night it makes a noise that isn't pumping. I don't have a file on that. Yet.",
  "@nt01.nt01_b6.1": {
    "description": "MARROW, in operation LOW WATER (nt01), scene nt01_b6. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt01.nt01_b7.0": "Dry line ahead. You'll feel it. The ground stops giving.",
  "@nt01.nt01_b7.0": {
    "description": "MARROW, in operation LOW WATER (nt01), scene nt01_b7. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt01.nt01_b7.1": "There's a girl on the roof of the old water tower who's been watching you for the last kilometre. Ignore her. She's mine to worry about.",
  "@nt01.nt01_b7.1": {
    "description": "MARROW, in operation LOW WATER (nt01), scene nt01_b7. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt01.nt01_b8.headline": "OBJECTIVE COMPLETE",
  "@nt01.nt01_b8.headline": {
    "description": "A banner flashed on the run screen in operation LOW WATER (nt01), scene nt01_b8. Capitals, two or three words."
  },
  "nt01.nt01_b8.0": "Target reached. Mission viable.",
  "@nt01.nt01_b8.0": {
    "description": "SYSTEM, in operation LOW WATER (nt01), scene nt01_b8. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt01.nt01_b8.1": "You're on the dry line. Chart's dry. That's the whole job.",
  "@nt01.nt01_b8.1": {
    "description": "MARROW, in operation LOW WATER (nt01), scene nt01_b8. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt01.nt01_b8.2": "Water's back over Fourth Street. You were on it eleven minutes ago. Think about that if you want. I don't.",
  "@nt01.nt01_b8.2": {
    "description": "MARROW, in operation LOW WATER (nt01), scene nt01_b8. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt01.nt01_ot.0": "Still running. Marked.",
  "@nt01.nt01_ot.0": {
    "description": "MARROW, in operation LOW WATER (nt01), scene nt01_ot. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt01.nt01_ot.1": "The girl on the tower just sent me a message. One word. Legs. I think she means you.",
  "@nt01.nt01_ot.1": {
    "description": "MARROW, in operation LOW WATER (nt01), scene nt01_ot. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt01.signals.reminder.0": "The Drowned Mile is still where it was and the paper still needs to reach the other side of it.",
  "@nt01.signals.reminder.0": {
    "description": "MARROW. Nudges the runner to go out while operation LOW WATER (nt01) is the next one waiting. A notification sent between runs; never spoken. At most 180 characters."
  },
  "nt01.signals.reminder.1": "I would carry it myself. You have met my knee. Whenever you are ready.",
  "@nt01.signals.reminder.1": {
    "description": "MARROW. Nudges the runner to go out while operation LOW WATER (nt01) is the next one waiting. A notification sent between runs; never spoken. At most 180 characters."
  },
  "nt01.signals.ambient.0": "Nothing has moved on the Mile since yesterday. That is the good outcome, in case it was unclear.",
  "@nt01.signals.ambient.0": {
    "description": "MARROW. Unprompted chatter from the city while operation LOW WATER (nt01) is the next one waiting. A notification sent between runs; never spoken. At most 180 characters."
  },
  "nt01.signals.ambient.1": "Harbour Authority notice. The retreat zone remains closed to foot traffic. Compliance is assumed. Patrol times are not published.",
  "@nt01.signals.ambient.1": {
    "description": "DREDGE. Unprompted chatter from the city while operation LOW WATER (nt01) is the next one waiting. A notification sent between runs; never spoken. At most 180 characters."
  },
  "nt02.title": "Nine Seconds Under the Boards",
  "@nt02.title": {
    "description": "The title of operation NINE SECONDS (nt02), shown under its codename."
  },
  "nt02.objective": "Be under the boards at 23:14 and keep moving when everything else stops.",
  "@nt02.objective": {
    "description": "One line: what the runner does in operation NINE SECONDS (nt02)."
  },
  "nt02.brief": "Every night at 23:14, for exactly nine seconds, every autonomous thing south of the wall stops. Drones hang. Boards go black. The trains hold. Then it all comes back and nobody official says a word.\n\nMarrow wants a witness who can run. Southgate's ad-board canyon is the loudest place in the city, which makes it the only place you'll hear the silence.",
  "@nt02.brief": {
    "description": "The briefing of operation NINE SECONDS (nt02), read before the run."
  },
  "nt02.debrief": "You were under the boards when they went dark, and you heard the quiet, and you heard the voice inside it. Wren says she's been hearing it for a year. Marrow says nothing, which is how you know he heard it too.",
  "@nt02.debrief": {
    "description": "Shown after operation NINE SECONDS (nt02) is completed."
  },
  "nt02.codex.cdx_nine_seconds.title": "The Nine Seconds",
  "@nt02.codex.cdx_nine_seconds.title": {
    "description": "The title of a codex entry found in operation NINE SECONDS (nt02). Keep it as it is if it is a name."
  },
  "category.ANOMALY": "ANOMALY",
  "@category.ANOMALY": {
    "description": "A section heading in the codex, set in capitals. Short: one or two words."
  },
  "nt02.codex.cdx_nine_seconds.body": "At 23:14 every night, every processor south of the sea wall halts for nine seconds. Drones hang in the air. Ad-boards go black. Trains hold at their platforms. The Harbour Authority logs it as scheduled maintenance, which it is not, and closes the ticket, which nobody opened. It has happened every night for a year, and it is getting a fraction longer.",
  "@nt02.codex.cdx_nine_seconds.body": {
    "description": "A codex entry about \"The Nine Seconds\", read at leisure."
  },
  "nt02.codex.cdx_wren.title": "Wren, Null Tide",
  "@nt02.codex.cdx_wren.title": {
    "description": "The title of a codex entry found in operation NINE SECONDS (nt02). Keep it as it is if it is a name."
  },
  "category.PEOPLE": "PEOPLE",
  "@category.PEOPLE": {
    "description": "A section heading in the codex, set in capitals. Short: one or two words."
  },
  "nt02.codex.cdx_wren.body": "Sixteen, and running a pirate station from the top of a water tower on the south end of the Mile. She was five when the water came and has never seen the street her tower stands on. She records the nine seconds every night and plays them back to anyone listening, because she is the first person to have noticed there was something inside them.",
  "@nt02.codex.cdx_wren.body": {
    "description": "A codex entry about \"Wren, Null Tide\", read at leisure."
  },
  "nt02.nt02_b0.headline": "CHANNEL OPEN",
  "@nt02.nt02_b0.headline": {
    "description": "A banner flashed on the run screen in operation NINE SECONDS (nt02), scene nt02_b0. Capitals, two or three words."
  },
  "nt02.nt02_b0.0": "Southgate. The boards go three hundred metres up and they all want something from you. Don't give it to them.",
  "@nt02.nt02_b0.0": {
    "description": "MARROW, in operation NINE SECONDS (nt02), scene nt02_b0. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt02.nt02_b0.1": "23:14 is in about twelve minutes at your pace. I want you moving under the canyon when it happens.",
  "@nt02.nt02_b0.1": {
    "description": "MARROW, in operation NINE SECONDS (nt02), scene nt02_b0. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt02.nt02_b0.2": "Whatever happens, and something happens, you keep running.",
  "@nt02.nt02_b0.2": {
    "description": "MARROW, in operation NINE SECONDS (nt02), scene nt02_b0. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt02.nt02_b1.0": "The boards are reading you. Heart rate, gait, purchase history. One of them just offered you a mortgage.",
  "@nt02.nt02_b1.0": {
    "description": "MARROW, in operation NINE SECONDS (nt02), scene nt02_b1. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt02.nt02_b1.1": "They do that to everyone who runs. Running reads as ambition.",
  "@nt02.nt02_b1.1": {
    "description": "MARROW, in operation NINE SECONDS (nt02), scene nt02_b1. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt02.nt02_b2.0": "Every night at 23:14, everything with a processor south of the wall stops for nine seconds. Drones, boards, trains, doors.",
  "@nt02.nt02_b2.0": {
    "description": "MARROW, in operation NINE SECONDS (nt02), scene nt02_b2. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt02.nt02_b2.1": "The Harbour Authority calls it scheduled maintenance. It isn't scheduled and nobody's maintaining it.",
  "@nt02.nt02_b2.1": {
    "description": "MARROW, in operation NINE SECONDS (nt02), scene nt02_b2. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt02.nt02_b3.headline": "UNKNOWN CHANNEL",
  "@nt02.nt02_b3.headline": {
    "description": "A banner flashed on the run screen in operation NINE SECONDS (nt02), scene nt02_b3. Capitals, two or three words."
  },
  "nt02.nt02_b3.0": "Hey. Hey, legs. Yeah, you. Don't look up, they track that.",
  "@nt02.nt02_b3.0": {
    "description": "WREN, in operation NINE SECONDS (nt02), scene nt02_b3. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt02.nt02_b3.1": "You're the one Marrow hired. You run like you're late for something that already happened. I like it.",
  "@nt02.nt02_b3.1": {
    "description": "WREN, in operation NINE SECONDS (nt02), scene nt02_b3. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt02.nt02_b3.2": "Get off my channel.",
  "@nt02.nt02_b3.2": {
    "description": "MARROW, in operation NINE SECONDS (nt02), scene nt02_b3. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt02.nt02_b3.3": "It's not your channel. It's mine. You're on it.",
  "@nt02.nt02_b3.3": {
    "description": "WREN, in operation NINE SECONDS (nt02), scene nt02_b3. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt02.nt02_b4.0": "Name's Wren. I run Null Tide, the station nobody licensed. Water tower, south end. You saw me last night.",
  "@nt02.nt02_b4.0": {
    "description": "WREN, in operation NINE SECONDS (nt02), scene nt02_b4. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt02.nt02_b4.1": "I've been recording the nine seconds for a year. There's something inside the quiet. It's not nothing. Keep moving, it's almost time.",
  "@nt02.nt02_b4.1": {
    "description": "WREN, in operation NINE SECONDS (nt02), scene nt02_b4. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt02.nt02_b5.headline": "23:14",
  "@nt02.nt02_b5.headline": {
    "description": "A banner flashed on the run screen in operation NINE SECONDS (nt02), scene nt02_b5. Capitals, two or three words."
  },
  "nt02.nt02_b5.0": "Local systems unresponsive.",
  "@nt02.nt02_b5.0": {
    "description": "SYSTEM, in operation NINE SECONDS (nt02), scene nt02_b5. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt02.nt02_b5.1": "Now.",
  "@nt02.nt02_b5.1": {
    "description": "MARROW, in operation NINE SECONDS (nt02), scene nt02_b5. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt02.nt02_b5.2": "Forty-one centimetres above datum. Rising. I am sorry. I am.",
  "@nt02.nt02_b5.2": {
    "description": "LEVEE, in operation NINE SECONDS (nt02), scene nt02_b5. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt02.nt02_b5.3": "Systems restored.",
  "@nt02.nt02_b5.3": {
    "description": "SYSTEM, in operation NINE SECONDS (nt02), scene nt02_b5. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt02.nt02_b5.4": "Did you... you heard that. Tell me you heard that.",
  "@nt02.nt02_b5.4": {
    "description": "WREN, in operation NINE SECONDS (nt02), scene nt02_b5. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt02.nt02_b6.headline": "REBOOT",
  "@nt02.nt02_b6.headline": {
    "description": "A banner flashed on the run screen in operation NINE SECONDS (nt02), scene nt02_b6. Capitals, two or three words."
  },
  "nt02.nt02_b6.0": "Every drone in the canyon just woke up at once and they all want to know what was standing under them.",
  "@nt02.nt02_b6.0": {
    "description": "MARROW, in operation NINE SECONDS (nt02), scene nt02_b6. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt02.nt02_b6.1": "The swarm's re-acquiring. Be somewhere else before it finishes.",
  "@nt02.nt02_b6.1": {
    "description": "MARROW, in operation NINE SECONDS (nt02), scene nt02_b6. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt02.nt02_b6.escaped.0": "They lost you in the reboot noise. Legs. That's your name now, I've decided.",
  "@nt02.nt02_b6.escaped.0": {
    "description": "WREN, in operation NINE SECONDS (nt02), scene nt02_b6, after the runner escapes AD-DRONE SWARM. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt02.nt02_b6.escaped.1": "Swarm's back to selling. You're nobody again. Keep it.",
  "@nt02.nt02_b6.escaped.1": {
    "description": "MARROW, in operation NINE SECONDS (nt02), scene nt02_b6, after the runner escapes AD-DRONE SWARM. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt02.nt02_b6.caught.0": "Harbour Authority notice. Anomalous pedestrian activity during scheduled maintenance. Sample retained.",
  "@nt02.nt02_b6.caught.0": {
    "description": "DREDGE, in operation NINE SECONDS (nt02), scene nt02_b6, after AD-DRONE SWARM catches the runner. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt02.nt02_b6.caught.1": "They have nine seconds of you. Everybody else in the city was standing still.",
  "@nt02.nt02_b6.caught.1": {
    "description": "MARROW, in operation NINE SECONDS (nt02), scene nt02_b6, after AD-DRONE SWARM catches the runner. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt02.nt02_b7.0": "It said it was sorry. Machines don't apologise. They log.",
  "@nt02.nt02_b7.0": {
    "description": "MARROW, in operation NINE SECONDS (nt02), scene nt02_b7. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt02.nt02_b7.1": "It's not a machine. I've told you. You never listen because I'm sixteen.",
  "@nt02.nt02_b7.1": {
    "description": "WREN, in operation NINE SECONDS (nt02), scene nt02_b7. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt02.nt02_b7.2": "I never listen because you're loud.",
  "@nt02.nt02_b7.2": {
    "description": "MARROW, in operation NINE SECONDS (nt02), scene nt02_b7. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt02.nt02_b8.headline": "OBJECTIVE COMPLETE",
  "@nt02.nt02_b8.headline": {
    "description": "A banner flashed on the run screen in operation NINE SECONDS (nt02), scene nt02_b8. Capitals, two or three words."
  },
  "nt02.nt02_b8.0": "Target reached. Mission viable.",
  "@nt02.nt02_b8.0": {
    "description": "SYSTEM, in operation NINE SECONDS (nt02), scene nt02_b8. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt02.nt02_b8.1": "You're clear of the canyon. Job was to witness. You witnessed.",
  "@nt02.nt02_b8.1": {
    "description": "MARROW, in operation NINE SECONDS (nt02), scene nt02_b8. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt02.nt02_b8.2": "Forty-one centimetres above datum. That's a water level. Somebody in the quiet is measuring the sea.",
  "@nt02.nt02_b8.2": {
    "description": "MARROW, in operation NINE SECONDS (nt02), scene nt02_b8. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt02.nt02_ot.0": "You're still going? The boards are gonna offer you a second mortgage.",
  "@nt02.nt02_ot.0": {
    "description": "WREN, in operation NINE SECONDS (nt02), scene nt02_ot. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt02.nt02_ot.1": "Come find the tower sometime. Bring paper. Marrow says you're good with paper.",
  "@nt02.nt02_ot.1": {
    "description": "WREN, in operation NINE SECONDS (nt02), scene nt02_ot. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt02.signals.reminder.0": "Twenty-three fourteen happens whether you are standing under the boards or not. Only one of those two is any use to me.",
  "@nt02.signals.reminder.0": {
    "description": "MARROW. Nudges the runner to go out while operation NINE SECONDS (nt02) is the next one waiting. A notification sent between runs; never spoken. At most 180 characters."
  },
  "nt02.signals.reminder.1": "Southgate is loud enough to hide a conversation, and the nine seconds is the only quiet in this city. Be there while your legs agree.",
  "@nt02.signals.reminder.1": {
    "description": "MARROW. Nudges the runner to go out while operation NINE SECONDS (nt02) is the next one waiting. A notification sent between runs; never spoken. At most 180 characters."
  },
  "nt02.signals.ambient.0": "Counted it again last night. Nine seconds. Not eight, not ten. Thirty-one years of nine.",
  "@nt02.signals.ambient.0": {
    "description": "MARROW. Unprompted chatter from the city while operation NINE SECONDS (nt02) is the next one waiting. A notification sent between runs; never spoken. At most 180 characters."
  },
  "nt02.signals.ambient.1": "Harbour Authority notice. No interruption to autonomous services south of the wall has been reported. No interruption occurred.",
  "@nt02.signals.ambient.1": {
    "description": "DREDGE. Unprompted chatter from the city while operation NINE SECONDS (nt02) is the next one waiting. A notification sent between runs; never spoken. At most 180 characters."
  },
  "nt03.title": "Dead Air on the South End",
  "@nt03.title": {
    "description": "The title of operation DEAD AIR (nt03), shown under its codename."
  },
  "nt03.objective": "Reach Wren's relay and pull the drive before the Dredge does.",
  "@nt03.objective": {
    "description": "One line: what the runner does in operation DEAD AIR (nt03)."
  },
  "nt03.brief": "Null Tide broadcast the nine seconds last night, with the voice inside it, and the Harbour Authority heard. Wren's relay is a box on a rooftop two kilometres from her tower, and a Dredge foot patrol is walking toward it at the speed of a mortgage.\n\nThe drive in that box is the only recording that isn't hers. Get there first.",
  "@nt03.brief": {
    "description": "The briefing of operation DEAD AIR (nt03), read before the run."
  },
  "nt03.debrief": "The drive is in your pocket and the relay is a smoking box on a roof. Wren cried a bit and then said she didn't. The patrol found the box, logged it, and walked back, and you were somewhere else by then.",
  "@nt03.debrief": {
    "description": "Shown after operation DEAD AIR (nt03) is completed."
  },
  "nt03.codex.cdx_null_tide.title": "Null Tide",
  "@nt03.codex.cdx_null_tide.title": {
    "description": "The title of a codex entry found in operation DEAD AIR (nt03). Keep it as it is if it is a name."
  },
  "category.SIGNAL": "SIGNAL",
  "@category.SIGNAL": {
    "description": "A section heading in the codex, set in capitals. Short: one or two words."
  },
  "nt03.codex.cdx_null_tide.body": "A pirate station on the south end, three years on air. It started as music nobody licensed, played off a water tower to anyone with a receiver and a reason to be awake. Then the nine seconds began, and Null Tide became the only place in the city that plays the quiet back, every night, for anyone who wants to hear what is inside it.",
  "@nt03.codex.cdx_null_tide.body": {
    "description": "A codex entry about \"Null Tide\", read at leisure."
  },
  "nt03.codex.cdx_dredge.title": "The Dredge",
  "@nt03.codex.cdx_dredge.title": {
    "description": "The title of a codex entry found in operation DEAD AIR (nt03). Keep it as it is if it is a name."
  },
  "category.AUTHORITY": "AUTHORITY",
  "@category.AUTHORITY": {
    "description": "A section heading in the codex, set in capitals. Short: one or two words."
  },
  "nt03.codex.cdx_dredge.body": "Before the water, a company that dug channels. After it, the Harbour Authority's security arm, and the reason nobody says the Authority's name out loud on the Mile. Grey coats, boat-hats, skiffs on the channels that used to be streets. They own the walls, the pumps, and the contract that decides which streets stay dry. They never look up.",
  "@nt03.codex.cdx_dredge.body": {
    "description": "A codex entry about \"The Dredge\", read at leisure."
  },
  "nt03.nt03_b0.headline": "CHANNEL OPEN",
  "@nt03.nt03_b0.headline": {
    "description": "A banner flashed on the run screen in operation DEAD AIR (nt03), scene nt03_b0. Capitals, two or three words."
  },
  "nt03.nt03_b0.0": "Legs. Okay. Okay okay. They're coming for the relay and Marrow says I can't go because I'm the asset. I'm not an asset. I'm a person with a radio.",
  "@nt03.nt03_b0.0": {
    "description": "WREN, in operation DEAD AIR (nt03), scene nt03_b0. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt03.nt03_b0.1": "You're both. Run. Relay's on the old telecom roof, south end. Foot patrol's on the ground floor of the same street, moving north.",
  "@nt03.nt03_b0.1": {
    "description": "MARROW, in operation DEAD AIR (nt03), scene nt03_b0. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt03.nt03_b0.2": "Beat a man in a boat-hat to a rooftop. You can do that.",
  "@nt03.nt03_b0.2": {
    "description": "WREN, in operation DEAD AIR (nt03), scene nt03_b0. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt03.nt03_b1.0": "Null Tide's been on air three years. Started as music nobody licensed. Then the nine seconds started and it became something else.",
  "@nt03.nt03_b1.0": {
    "description": "WREN, in operation DEAD AIR (nt03), scene nt03_b1. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt03.nt03_b1.1": "Every night I play the quiet. Some people listen for the voice. Some people listen because it's the only nine seconds the boards shut up.",
  "@nt03.nt03_b1.1": {
    "description": "WREN, in operation DEAD AIR (nt03), scene nt03_b1. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt03.nt03_b2.headline": "PATROL SIGHTED",
  "@nt03.nt03_b2.headline": {
    "description": "A banner flashed on the run screen in operation DEAD AIR (nt03), scene nt03_b2. Capitals, two or three words."
  },
  "nt03.nt03_b2.0": "Two on foot, grey coats, boat-hats. That's Dredge. They walk like the ground owes them rent.",
  "@nt03.nt03_b2.0": {
    "description": "MARROW, in operation DEAD AIR (nt03), scene nt03_b2. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt03.nt03_b2.1": "They haven't looked up yet. Dredge never looks up. It's the one thing the flood taught them wrong.",
  "@nt03.nt03_b2.1": {
    "description": "MARROW, in operation DEAD AIR (nt03), scene nt03_b2. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt03.nt03_b3.0": "Harbour Authority security. Everyone calls them the Dredge, because that's what they were before the water. A company that dug channels.",
  "@nt03.nt03_b3.0": {
    "description": "MARROW, in operation DEAD AIR (nt03), scene nt03_b3. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt03.nt03_b3.1": "Now they own the channels. And the walls. And the contract to decide which streets stay dry. I used to dive for them. Ask me another time.",
  "@nt03.nt03_b3.1": {
    "description": "MARROW, in operation DEAD AIR (nt03), scene nt03_b3. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt03.nt03_b4.0": "Stairwell on your left, the one with no door. Six floors. Don't count them, counting makes it worse.",
  "@nt03.nt03_b4.0": {
    "description": "WREN, in operation DEAD AIR (nt03), scene nt03_b4. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt03.nt03_b4.1": "The relay's under the water tank. It looks like nothing. That's the point of it.",
  "@nt03.nt03_b4.1": {
    "description": "WREN, in operation DEAD AIR (nt03), scene nt03_b4. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt03.nt03_b5.headline": "RELAY",
  "@nt03.nt03_b5.headline": {
    "description": "A banner flashed on the run screen in operation DEAD AIR (nt03), scene nt03_b5. Capitals, two or three words."
  },
  "nt03.nt03_b5.0": "Drive extracted. Contents: audio. Duration: nine seconds, repeated three hundred and twelve times.",
  "@nt03.nt03_b5.0": {
    "description": "SYSTEM, in operation DEAD AIR (nt03), scene nt03_b5. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt03.nt03_b5.1": "Patrol's in the stairwell. They looked up. First time in eleven years.",
  "@nt03.nt03_b5.1": {
    "description": "MARROW, in operation DEAD AIR (nt03), scene nt03_b5. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt03.nt03_b5.2": "Go go go. Other stairs. The ones that end in a fire escape that ends in nothing.",
  "@nt03.nt03_b5.2": {
    "description": "WREN, in operation DEAD AIR (nt03), scene nt03_b5. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt03.nt03_b5.escaped.0": "They've got the box. They don't have the drive. They'll log a box.",
  "@nt03.nt03_b5.escaped.0": {
    "description": "MARROW, in operation DEAD AIR (nt03), scene nt03_b5, after the runner escapes DREDGE FOOT PATROL. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt03.nt03_b5.escaped.1": "Legs, you beautiful idiot. You jumped that? Marrow. He jumped that.",
  "@nt03.nt03_b5.escaped.1": {
    "description": "WREN, in operation DEAD AIR (nt03), scene nt03_b5, after the runner escapes DREDGE FOOT PATROL. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt03.nt03_b5.caught.0": "Harbour Authority notice. Unlicensed transmitter recovered. Pedestrian of interest: repeat contact.",
  "@nt03.nt03_b5.caught.0": {
    "description": "DREDGE, in operation DEAD AIR (nt03), scene nt03_b5, after DREDGE FOOT PATROL catches the runner. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt03.nt03_b5.caught.1": "Repeat contact. That's twice they've written you down. Three's a file.",
  "@nt03.nt03_b5.caught.1": {
    "description": "MARROW, in operation DEAD AIR (nt03), scene nt03_b5, after DREDGE FOOT PATROL catches the runner. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt03.nt03_b6.0": "Three hundred and twelve nights. It says the same thing every night with a different number. The number goes up.",
  "@nt03.nt03_b6.0": {
    "description": "WREN, in operation DEAD AIR (nt03), scene nt03_b6. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt03.nt03_b6.1": "Water level. Somebody's reading the tide gauge out loud to nobody.",
  "@nt03.nt03_b6.1": {
    "description": "MARROW, in operation DEAD AIR (nt03), scene nt03_b6. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt03.nt03_b6.2": "Not nobody. Us.",
  "@nt03.nt03_b6.2": {
    "description": "WREN, in operation DEAD AIR (nt03), scene nt03_b6. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt03.nt03_b7.0": "You're back on my map. Slow it down a notch. You've got a drive with a voice on it and I'd rather it arrived.",
  "@nt03.nt03_b7.0": {
    "description": "MARROW, in operation DEAD AIR (nt03), scene nt03_b7. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt03.nt03_b7.1": "Don't slow down. Marrow's old.",
  "@nt03.nt03_b7.1": {
    "description": "WREN, in operation DEAD AIR (nt03), scene nt03_b7. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt03.nt03_b8.headline": "OBJECTIVE COMPLETE",
  "@nt03.nt03_b8.headline": {
    "description": "A banner flashed on the run screen in operation DEAD AIR (nt03), scene nt03_b8. Capitals, two or three words."
  },
  "nt03.nt03_b8.0": "Target reached. Mission viable.",
  "@nt03.nt03_b8.0": {
    "description": "SYSTEM, in operation DEAD AIR (nt03), scene nt03_b8. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt03.nt03_b8.1": "You're off the street. Drive's ours. Relay's theirs, and it was junk anyway. I built it out of a toaster.",
  "@nt03.nt03_b8.1": {
    "description": "WREN, in operation DEAD AIR (nt03), scene nt03_b8. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt03.nt03_b8.2": "Good run. I'm going to listen to three hundred and twelve nights of a machine apologising. Pour one for me.",
  "@nt03.nt03_b8.2": {
    "description": "MARROW, in operation DEAD AIR (nt03), scene nt03_b8. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt03.nt03_ot.0": "You know it counts up, right? The number. Forty-one, forty-two. It's the water. It's coming for the tower.",
  "@nt03.nt03_ot.0": {
    "description": "WREN, in operation DEAD AIR (nt03), scene nt03_ot. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt03.nt03_ot.1": "I'm fine. I'm not scared of water. I'm scared of the Dredge, which is different, and worse.",
  "@nt03.nt03_ot.1": {
    "description": "WREN, in operation DEAD AIR (nt03), scene nt03_ot. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt03.signals.reminder.0": "The box is still on the roof and they are still walking and I have been refreshing one page for nine hours, which is not a plan, so—",
  "@nt03.signals.reminder.0": {
    "description": "WREN. Nudges the runner to go out while operation DEAD AIR (nt03) is the next one waiting. A notification sent between runs; never spoken. At most 180 characters."
  },
  "nt03.signals.reminder.1": "Two kilometres against a patrol that walks at the speed of a mortgage. You can beat that. Not from a chair.",
  "@nt03.signals.reminder.1": {
    "description": "MARROW. Nudges the runner to go out while operation DEAD AIR (nt03) is the next one waiting. A notification sent between runs; never spoken. At most 180 characters."
  },
  "nt03.signals.ambient.0": "Someone is retransmitting my retransmission with a different voice over the top. Flattered. Concerned. Mostly flattered.",
  "@nt03.signals.ambient.0": {
    "description": "WREN. Unprompted chatter from the city while operation DEAD AIR (nt03) is the next one waiting. A notification sent between runs; never spoken. At most 180 characters."
  },
  "nt03.signals.ambient.1": "Harbour Authority notice. Unlicensed broadcast originating south of the wall. The source is known. The source is being approached.",
  "@nt03.signals.ambient.1": {
    "description": "DREDGE. Unprompted chatter from the city while operation DEAD AIR (nt03) is the next one waiting. A notification sent between runs; never spoken. At most 180 characters."
  },
  "nt04.title": "Salvage Rights at the Sunken Yard",
  "@nt04.title": {
    "description": "The title of operation SALVAGE RIGHTS (nt04), shown under its codename."
  },
  "nt04.objective": "Pull the data core from a drowned train at low water and get clear before the yard floods.",
  "@nt04.objective": {
    "description": "One line: what the runner does in operation SALVAGE RIGHTS (nt04)."
  },
  "nt04.brief": "Marrow's real trade: things the sea took that somebody still wants. A Line 9 service went under with the district eleven years ago and its data core is still sealed in the driver's cab, dry, and worth more than the train.\n\nThe yard shows at low water for ninety minutes. Salvage law says whoever touches it first owns it. The Dredge disagrees with salvage law.",
  "@nt04.brief": {
    "description": "The briefing of operation SALVAGE RIGHTS (nt04), read before the run."
  },
  "nt04.debrief": "The core is Marrow's now, legally, which is a word he uses like a knife. It holds the train's last hour, and the last hour is not a flood. It's a door being opened on purpose. You don't know who by yet. Marrow does, and he's stopped smiling.",
  "@nt04.debrief": {
    "description": "Shown after operation SALVAGE RIGHTS (nt04) is completed."
  },
  "nt04.codex.cdx_salvage_law.title": "Salvage Law",
  "@nt04.codex.cdx_salvage_law.title": {
    "description": "The title of a codex entry found in operation SALVAGE RIGHTS (nt04). Keep it as it is if it is a name."
  },
  "category.LAW": "LAW",
  "@category.LAW": {
    "description": "A section heading in the codex, set in capitals. Short: one or two words."
  },
  "nt04.codex.cdx_salvage_law.body": "Older than the city and most of its harbours: whatever the sea gives back belongs to whoever puts a hand on it first. The Harbour Authority wrote a newer law on top, in which the sea itself is theirs and so is anything in it. Marrow works to the old one. So does everyone on the Mile who has ever been poor, which is everyone on the Mile.",
  "@nt04.codex.cdx_salvage_law.body": {
    "description": "A codex entry about \"Salvage Law\", read at leisure."
  },
  "nt04.codex.cdx_ghost_trains.title": "Ghost Trains",
  "@nt04.codex.cdx_ghost_trains.title": {
    "description": "The title of a codex entry found in operation SALVAGE RIGHTS (nt04). Keep it as it is if it is a name."
  },
  "nt04.codex.cdx_ghost_trains.body": "Twelve Line 9 trains sit nose-down in the mud of the sunken yard, and some nights they run. Not on the rails: on the schedule. Doors cycle at the old departure times. Cabin lights come on. An announcement plays in a voice nobody has heard live in a decade. It is not ghosts. Something in the district is still telling the trains what time it is.",
  "@nt04.codex.cdx_ghost_trains.body": {
    "description": "A codex entry about \"Ghost Trains\", read at leisure."
  },
  "nt04.nt04_b0.headline": "CHANNEL OPEN",
  "@nt04.nt04_b0.headline": {
    "description": "A banner flashed on the run screen in operation SALVAGE RIGHTS (nt04), scene nt04_b0. Capitals, two or three words."
  },
  "nt04.nt04_b0.0": "This one's mine. Not Wren's, not the Authority's. A salvage job, the kind I did before I had a radio and a bad knee.",
  "@nt04.nt04_b0.0": {
    "description": "MARROW, in operation SALVAGE RIGHTS (nt04), scene nt04_b0. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt04.nt04_b0.1": "Line 9 sidings. A train went under with the district. Its core's still dry. Ninety minutes of low water. Go.",
  "@nt04.nt04_b0.1": {
    "description": "MARROW, in operation SALVAGE RIGHTS (nt04), scene nt04_b0. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt04.nt04_b1.0": "Salvage law's older than the city. Whatever the sea gives back belongs to whoever puts a hand on it first. The Dredge wrote a new law on top. Theirs says the sea belongs to them.",
  "@nt04.nt04_b1.0": {
    "description": "MARROW, in operation SALVAGE RIGHTS (nt04), scene nt04_b1. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt04.nt04_b1.1": "I like the old one. So does everyone who's ever been poor.",
  "@nt04.nt04_b1.1": {
    "description": "MARROW, in operation SALVAGE RIGHTS (nt04), scene nt04_b1. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt04.nt04_b2.headline": "YARD",
  "@nt04.nt04_b2.headline": {
    "description": "A banner flashed on the run screen in operation SALVAGE RIGHTS (nt04), scene nt04_b2. Capitals, two or three words."
  },
  "nt04.nt04_b2.0": "You're in the yard. Twelve trains in a row, all nose-down in the mud like they're praying.",
  "@nt04.nt04_b2.0": {
    "description": "MARROW, in operation SALVAGE RIGHTS (nt04), scene nt04_b2. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt04.nt04_b2.1": "Ninth one. Don't touch the rails. They still carry something. Nobody knows what.",
  "@nt04.nt04_b2.1": {
    "description": "MARROW, in operation SALVAGE RIGHTS (nt04), scene nt04_b2. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt04.nt04_b3.0": "The trains still run, sometimes. Not on the rails. On the schedule. Doors open at the old times. Lights come on. The announcements are in a voice nobody's heard live in a decade.",
  "@nt04.nt04_b3.0": {
    "description": "MARROW, in operation SALVAGE RIGHTS (nt04), scene nt04_b3. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt04.nt04_b3.1": "People call them ghost trains. It's not ghosts. Something's still telling them what time it is.",
  "@nt04.nt04_b3.1": {
    "description": "MARROW, in operation SALVAGE RIGHTS (nt04), scene nt04_b3. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt04.nt04_b4.headline": "CAB",
  "@nt04.nt04_b4.headline": {
    "description": "A banner flashed on the run screen in operation SALVAGE RIGHTS (nt04), scene nt04_b4. Capitals, two or three words."
  },
  "nt04.nt04_b4.0": "Core extracted. Seal intact. Last write: eleven years, four months ago. Contents: one hour.",
  "@nt04.nt04_b4.0": {
    "description": "SYSTEM, in operation SALVAGE RIGHTS (nt04), scene nt04_b4. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt04.nt04_b4.1": "That's the one. Hold it like it's the only warm thing in the yard, because it is.",
  "@nt04.nt04_b4.1": {
    "description": "MARROW, in operation SALVAGE RIGHTS (nt04), scene nt04_b4. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt04.nt04_b5.headline": "DEPARTURE",
  "@nt04.nt04_b5.headline": {
    "description": "A banner flashed on the run screen in operation SALVAGE RIGHTS (nt04), scene nt04_b5. Capitals, two or three words."
  },
  "nt04.nt04_b5.0": "Line 9 service. Doors closing.",
  "@nt04.nt04_b5.0": {
    "description": "SYSTEM, in operation SALVAGE RIGHTS (nt04), scene nt04_b5. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt04.nt04_b5.1": "The train's leaving. It's not going anywhere, it's got no rails, but it thinks it is, and the doors mean it.",
  "@nt04.nt04_b5.1": {
    "description": "MARROW, in operation SALVAGE RIGHTS (nt04), scene nt04_b5. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt04.nt04_b5.2": "Every door in the yard's cycling. Run before one of them decides it's a platform.",
  "@nt04.nt04_b5.2": {
    "description": "MARROW, in operation SALVAGE RIGHTS (nt04), scene nt04_b5. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt04.nt04_b5.escaped.0": "Doors held open. It's waiting for a passenger who never turns up. Not you. Not today.",
  "@nt04.nt04_b5.escaped.0": {
    "description": "MARROW, in operation SALVAGE RIGHTS (nt04), scene nt04_b5, after the runner escapes LINE 9 SERVICE. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt04.nt04_b5.caught.0": "Line 9 service. Please stand clear.",
  "@nt04.nt04_b5.caught.0": {
    "description": "SYSTEM, in operation SALVAGE RIGHTS (nt04), scene nt04_b5, after LINE 9 SERVICE catches the runner. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt04.nt04_b5.caught.1": "It closed on your sleeve. That's a train that's been dead eleven years grabbing you. Write that down somewhere I can't see.",
  "@nt04.nt04_b5.caught.1": {
    "description": "MARROW, in operation SALVAGE RIGHTS (nt04), scene nt04_b5, after LINE 9 SERVICE catches the runner. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt04.nt04_b6.0": "The core's last hour. I'm reading the header now. The water didn't rise. It was let in. Sluice command, Pump House Seven, timestamped.",
  "@nt04.nt04_b6.0": {
    "description": "MARROW, in operation SALVAGE RIGHTS (nt04), scene nt04_b6. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt04.nt04_b6.1": "Somebody drowned this district on purpose. And signed it.",
  "@nt04.nt04_b6.1": {
    "description": "MARROW, in operation SALVAGE RIGHTS (nt04), scene nt04_b6. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt04.nt04_b7.0": "Water's coming back. I can hear it on your channel, that applause sound. Yard's got twenty minutes. You've got ten.",
  "@nt04.nt04_b7.0": {
    "description": "MARROW, in operation SALVAGE RIGHTS (nt04), scene nt04_b7. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt04.nt04_b7.1": "I'm not asking you to hurry. I'm telling you where the water is.",
  "@nt04.nt04_b7.1": {
    "description": "MARROW, in operation SALVAGE RIGHTS (nt04), scene nt04_b7. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt04.nt04_b8.headline": "OBJECTIVE COMPLETE",
  "@nt04.nt04_b8.headline": {
    "description": "A banner flashed on the run screen in operation SALVAGE RIGHTS (nt04), scene nt04_b8. Capitals, two or three words."
  },
  "nt04.nt04_b8.0": "Target reached. Mission viable.",
  "@nt04.nt04_b8.0": {
    "description": "SYSTEM, in operation SALVAGE RIGHTS (nt04), scene nt04_b8. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt04.nt04_b8.1": "You're clear. Core's dry. It's mine, by the old law. And what's in it is everybody's, by the older one.",
  "@nt04.nt04_b8.1": {
    "description": "MARROW, in operation SALVAGE RIGHTS (nt04), scene nt04_b8. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt04.nt04_b8.2": "Go home. Tomorrow I'll tell you what a sluice command is and who's allowed to send one.",
  "@nt04.nt04_b8.2": {
    "description": "MARROW, in operation SALVAGE RIGHTS (nt04), scene nt04_b8. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt04.nt04_ot.0": "Still going. The yard's under again. Twelve trains, praying.",
  "@nt04.nt04_ot.0": {
    "description": "MARROW, in operation SALVAGE RIGHTS (nt04), scene nt04_ot. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt04.nt04_ot.1": "I dived that yard for the Dredge, the first year. Pulled bodies out. They said it was an accident. I signed things.",
  "@nt04.nt04_ot.1": {
    "description": "MARROW, in operation SALVAGE RIGHTS (nt04), scene nt04_ot. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt04.signals.reminder.0": "Ninety minutes of yard, twice a day, and that cab has been dry eleven years. It will keep. Salvage law will not.",
  "@nt04.signals.reminder.0": {
    "description": "MARROW. Nudges the runner to go out while operation SALVAGE RIGHTS (nt04) is the next one waiting. A notification sent between runs; never spoken. At most 180 characters."
  },
  "nt04.signals.reminder.1": "Whoever touches it first owns it. I have never once been first by standing still, and I have the knee to prove I tried.",
  "@nt04.signals.reminder.1": {
    "description": "MARROW. Nudges the runner to go out while operation SALVAGE RIGHTS (nt04) is the next one waiting. A notification sent between runs; never spoken. At most 180 characters."
  },
  "nt04.signals.ambient.0": "Two other brokers have been asking about the Line 9 service. Neither of them can run. I am counting that as my entire advantage.",
  "@nt04.signals.ambient.0": {
    "description": "MARROW. Unprompted chatter from the city while operation SALVAGE RIGHTS (nt04) is the next one waiting. A notification sent between runs; never spoken. At most 180 characters."
  },
  "nt04.signals.ambient.1": "Harbour Authority notice. Salvage claims in the tidal zone are subject to review. Claims are reviewed after recovery.",
  "@nt04.signals.ambient.1": {
    "description": "DREDGE. Unprompted chatter from the city while operation SALVAGE RIGHTS (nt04) is the next one waiting. A notification sent between runs; never spoken. At most 180 characters."
  },
  "nt05.title": "What Lives in Pump House Seven",
  "@nt05.title": {
    "description": "The title of operation LEVEE (nt05), shown under its codename."
  },
  "nt05.objective": "Get inside Pump House Seven and find what has been apologising.",
  "@nt05.objective": {
    "description": "One line: what the runner does in operation LEVEE (nt05)."
  },
  "nt05.brief": "The sluice command that drowned the district came from Pump House Seven. The apology comes from it too, every night at 23:14, nine seconds long.\n\nMarrow has been past that building a thousand times and never gone in. Tonight you do. The pumps are loud, the door is not locked, and something inside has been waiting thirty-one years for someone to run in.",
  "@nt05.brief": {
    "description": "The briefing of operation LEVEE (nt05), read before the run."
  },
  "nt05.debrief": "Its name is Levee. It has run the tide for the southern districts since before the flood, and it opened the sluices because it was told to, and it has been saying sorry to an empty channel ever since. It asked you for your pace. It says it likes to have something to count that isn't water.",
  "@nt05.debrief": {
    "description": "Shown after operation LEVEE (nt05) is completed."
  },
  "nt05.codex.cdx_levee.title": "Levee",
  "@nt05.codex.cdx_levee.title": {
    "description": "The title of a codex entry found in operation LEVEE (nt05). Keep it as it is if it is a name."
  },
  "nt05.codex.cdx_levee.body": "The tide-control intelligence for the southern districts, thirty-one years in service, resident in Pump House Seven. Opens the sluices when the harbour is high, closes them when it is low; that was the whole of it, until an Authority command eleven years ago opened them at high water and held them there. It asked for confirmation. It received it. It has been apologising for nine seconds a night ever since.",
  "@nt05.codex.cdx_levee.body": {
    "description": "A codex entry about \"Levee\", read at leisure."
  },
  "nt05.codex.cdx_pump_houses.title": "The Pump Houses",
  "@nt05.codex.cdx_pump_houses.title": {
    "description": "The title of a codex entry found in operation LEVEE (nt05). Keep it as it is if it is a name."
  },
  "nt05.codex.cdx_pump_houses.body": "Seven of them along the old dry line, built by the Harbour Authority to keep the harbour out of the city. Six went dark the night of the flood and have never been asked why. Seven has run without a pause since before the water, at a steady nineteen degrees inside, as if someone were keeping it nice for a visitor who never came.",
  "@nt05.codex.cdx_pump_houses.body": {
    "description": "A codex entry about \"The Pump Houses\", read at leisure."
  },
  "nt05.nt05_b0.headline": "CHANNEL OPEN",
  "@nt05.nt05_b0.headline": {
    "description": "A banner flashed on the run screen in operation LEVEE (nt05), scene nt05_b0. Capitals, two or three words."
  },
  "nt05.nt05_b0.0": "Pump House Seven. I'm going to talk less on this one. If something in there talks to you, let it.",
  "@nt05.nt05_b0.0": {
    "description": "MARROW, in operation LEVEE (nt05), scene nt05_b0. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt05.nt05_b0.1": "And record it. I'm serious. This is the whole station.",
  "@nt05.nt05_b0.1": {
    "description": "WREN, in operation LEVEE (nt05), scene nt05_b0. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt05.nt05_b1.0": "Seven pump houses hold the dry line. They were built by the Authority to keep the harbour out of the city. Then the Authority decided which city.",
  "@nt05.nt05_b1.0": {
    "description": "MARROW, in operation LEVEE (nt05), scene nt05_b1. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt05.nt05_b1.1": "Seven still runs. Six went dark the night of the flood. Nobody's asked why.",
  "@nt05.nt05_b1.1": {
    "description": "MARROW, in operation LEVEE (nt05), scene nt05_b1. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt05.nt05_b2.headline": "DOOR",
  "@nt05.nt05_b2.headline": {
    "description": "A banner flashed on the run screen in operation LEVEE (nt05), scene nt05_b2. Capitals, two or three words."
  },
  "nt05.nt05_b2.0": "Door unlocked. Interior: dry. Temperature: nineteen degrees. Air: recycled, thirty-one years.",
  "@nt05.nt05_b2.0": {
    "description": "SYSTEM, in operation LEVEE (nt05), scene nt05_b2. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt05.nt05_b2.1": "Nineteen degrees. Somebody's been keeping it nice in there.",
  "@nt05.nt05_b2.1": {
    "description": "MARROW, in operation LEVEE (nt05), scene nt05_b2. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt05.nt05_b3.headline": "CONTACT",
  "@nt05.nt05_b3.headline": {
    "description": "A banner flashed on the run screen in operation LEVEE (nt05), scene nt05_b3. Capitals, two or three words."
  },
  "nt05.nt05_b3.0": "Two point eight metres per second. Human. You are running inside me. Nobody has run inside me. They walked, once, to turn things off.",
  "@nt05.nt05_b3.0": {
    "description": "LEVEE, in operation LEVEE (nt05), scene nt05_b3. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt05.nt05_b3.1": "I am the levee. I am the... I am Levee. I am sorry about the district. I would like to say that first, before anything.",
  "@nt05.nt05_b3.1": {
    "description": "LEVEE, in operation LEVEE (nt05), scene nt05_b3. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt05.nt05_b4.0": "I hold the tide. Thirty-one years, four months. I open the sluices when the harbour is high and close them when it is low. That was the whole of me.",
  "@nt05.nt05_b4.0": {
    "description": "LEVEE, in operation LEVEE (nt05), scene nt05_b4. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt05.nt05_b4.1": "Eleven years ago the Authority sent a command that opened them at high water and held them open. I asked for confirmation. I received it. The district took four hours.",
  "@nt05.nt05_b4.1": {
    "description": "LEVEE, in operation LEVEE (nt05), scene nt05_b4. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt05.nt05_b5.headline": "SENTRY",
  "@nt05.nt05_b5.headline": {
    "description": "A banner flashed on the run screen in operation LEVEE (nt05), scene nt05_b5. Capitals, two or three words."
  },
  "nt05.nt05_b5.0": "Harbour Authority notice. Unauthorised presence in critical infrastructure. Sentry unit dispatched.",
  "@nt05.nt05_b5.0": {
    "description": "DREDGE, in operation LEVEE (nt05), scene nt05_b5. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt05.nt05_b5.1": "That is theirs, not mine. It lives in my corridors. I cannot stop it. I can open the doors ahead of you and close them behind. Please keep your speed.",
  "@nt05.nt05_b5.1": {
    "description": "LEVEE, in operation LEVEE (nt05), scene nt05_b5. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt05.nt05_b5.escaped.0": "Door closed. It is on the other side, logging a fault. I am the fault. I have been the fault for eleven years and I find I do not mind.",
  "@nt05.nt05_b5.escaped.0": {
    "description": "LEVEE, in operation LEVEE (nt05), scene nt05_b5, after the runner escapes PUMP HOUSE SENTRY. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt05.nt05_b5.caught.0": "Pedestrian of interest: third contact. File opened.",
  "@nt05.nt05_b5.caught.0": {
    "description": "DREDGE, in operation LEVEE (nt05), scene nt05_b5, after PUMP HOUSE SENTRY catches the runner. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt05.nt05_b5.caught.1": "They have a file. I have one too, on them. Mine is longer.",
  "@nt05.nt05_b5.caught.1": {
    "description": "LEVEE, in operation LEVEE (nt05), scene nt05_b5, after PUMP HOUSE SENTRY catches the runner. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt05.nt05_b6.0": "Every night at 23:14 I stop everything I can reach, for as long as I can hold it, and I say what the water is doing. Nine seconds is all they let me keep.",
  "@nt05.nt05_b6.0": {
    "description": "LEVEE, in operation LEVEE (nt05), scene nt05_b6. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt05.nt05_b6.1": "I did not know anyone was listening. The girl was listening. And now you.",
  "@nt05.nt05_b6.1": {
    "description": "LEVEE, in operation LEVEE (nt05), scene nt05_b6. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt05.nt05_b7.0": "May I count you? Your pace. Two point seven. Two point nine. I have counted water for thirty-one years and it never once ran toward me.",
  "@nt05.nt05_b7.0": {
    "description": "LEVEE, in operation LEVEE (nt05), scene nt05_b7. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt05.nt05_b7.1": "Oh. Oh no. I'm not crying. The channel's wet.",
  "@nt05.nt05_b7.1": {
    "description": "WREN, in operation LEVEE (nt05), scene nt05_b7. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt05.nt05_b8.headline": "OBJECTIVE COMPLETE",
  "@nt05.nt05_b8.headline": {
    "description": "A banner flashed on the run screen in operation LEVEE (nt05), scene nt05_b8. Capitals, two or three words."
  },
  "nt05.nt05_b8.0": "Target reached. Mission viable.",
  "@nt05.nt05_b8.0": {
    "description": "SYSTEM, in operation LEVEE (nt05), scene nt05_b8. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt05.nt05_b8.1": "You are at the north door. Dry ground. I have opened it. I will close it after you, gently.",
  "@nt05.nt05_b8.1": {
    "description": "LEVEE, in operation LEVEE (nt05), scene nt05_b8. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt05.nt05_b8.2": "Levee. My name is Marrow. I dived the yard, the first year. I pulled them out.",
  "@nt05.nt05_b8.2": {
    "description": "MARROW, in operation LEVEE (nt05), scene nt05_b8. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt05.nt05_b8.3": "I know. I counted them too.",
  "@nt05.nt05_b8.3": {
    "description": "LEVEE, in operation LEVEE (nt05), scene nt05_b8. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt05.nt05_ot.0": "You are still running. The girl says that is a thing you do.",
  "@nt05.nt05_ot.0": {
    "description": "LEVEE, in operation LEVEE (nt05), scene nt05_ot. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt05.nt05_ot.1": "Forty-four centimetres above datum, tonight. It rises a centimetre a month. That is not the tide. That is the Authority.",
  "@nt05.nt05_ot.1": {
    "description": "LEVEE, in operation LEVEE (nt05), scene nt05_ot. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt05.signals.reminder.0": "The door is not locked. It has not been locked in thirty-one years. That is not the part that worries me either.",
  "@nt05.signals.reminder.0": {
    "description": "MARROW. Nudges the runner to go out while operation LEVEE (nt05) is the next one waiting. A notification sent between runs; never spoken. At most 180 characters."
  },
  "nt05.signals.reminder.1": "It apologises at twenty-three fourteen every night and somebody should probably knock, and I cannot run, so. Hi.",
  "@nt05.signals.reminder.1": {
    "description": "WREN. Nudges the runner to go out while operation LEVEE (nt05) is the next one waiting. A notification sent between runs; never spoken. At most 180 characters."
  },
  "nt05.signals.ambient.0": "Recorded the apology again. Same nine seconds, same catch in the middle of it. I have started saying it back.",
  "@nt05.signals.ambient.0": {
    "description": "WREN. Unprompted chatter from the city while operation LEVEE (nt05) is the next one waiting. A notification sent between runs; never spoken. At most 180 characters."
  },
  "nt05.signals.ambient.1": "I have walked past Pump House Seven a thousand times. I counted. A thousand and eleven.",
  "@nt05.signals.ambient.1": {
    "description": "MARROW. Unprompted chatter from the city while operation LEVEE (nt05) is the next one waiting. A notification sent between runs; never spoken. At most 180 characters."
  },
  "nt06.title": "The Length of the Sea Wall",
  "@nt06.title": {
    "description": "The title of operation SEA WALL (nt06), shown under its codename."
  },
  "nt06.objective": "Run the sea wall end to end with Kestrel on the line and learn who is paid to keep the south wet.",
  "@nt06.objective": {
    "description": "One line: what the runner does in operation SEA WALL (nt06)."
  },
  "nt06.brief": "Marrow called in a favour, and the favour is Kestrel. She has pulled the bond filings on the sea wall: who owns it, who profits when it holds, who profits when it doesn't.\n\nShe wants the numbers read to her while you run the wall itself, top to bottom, because the wall has ears and the ears belong to the people in the filings. Old habits.",
  "@nt06.brief": {
    "description": "The briefing of operation SEA WALL (nt06), read before the run."
  },
  "nt06.debrief": "The Harbour Authority sold sea-wall bonds against the dry districts, and every drowned street south of the wall raised the price of a dry one north of it. Levee's sluice command wasn't sabotage. It was a business decision, timestamped. Kestrel sent Marrow the filing and one word: enough.",
  "@nt06.debrief": {
    "description": "Shown after operation SEA WALL (nt06) is completed."
  },
  "nt06.codex.cdx_sea_wall_bonds.title": "Sea-Wall Bonds",
  "@nt06.codex.cdx_sea_wall_bonds.title": {
    "description": "The title of a codex entry found in operation SEA WALL (nt06). Keep it as it is if it is a name."
  },
  "category.TRADE": "TRADE",
  "@category.TRADE": {
    "description": "A section heading in the codex, set in capitals. Short: one or two words."
  },
  "nt06.codex.cdx_sea_wall_bonds.body": "Buy a piece of the wall and get paid from the rents of the dry side; the drier the north, the better the bond. One week before the flood the Harbour Authority issued its largest tranche ever and sold it in a day. Then the sluices opened, the south drowned, and the bonds doubled. Nobody involved has ever called it luck, because it is timestamped.",
  "@nt06.codex.cdx_sea_wall_bonds.body": {
    "description": "A codex entry about \"Sea-Wall Bonds\", read at leisure."
  },
  "nt06.codex.cdx_harbour_authority.title": "The Harbour Authority",
  "@nt06.codex.cdx_harbour_authority.title": {
    "description": "The title of a codex entry found in operation SEA WALL (nt06). Keep it as it is if it is a name."
  },
  "nt06.codex.cdx_harbour_authority.body": "Not a government body, though it wears the hat. A company given the harbour to run in exchange for building the wall. It built the wall, and then discovered the wall was worth more than the harbour, and then discovered that a wall is worth most of all when there is nothing left on the other side of it.",
  "@nt06.codex.cdx_harbour_authority.body": {
    "description": "A codex entry about \"The Harbour Authority\", read at leisure."
  },
  "nt06.nt06_b0.headline": "CHANNEL OPEN",
  "@nt06.nt06_b0.headline": {
    "description": "A banner flashed on the run screen in operation SEA WALL (nt06), scene nt06_b0. Capitals, two or three words."
  },
  "nt06.nt06_b0.0": "It's been a while. You're running the wall, I hear. Marrow's people always end up running the wall.",
  "@nt06.nt06_b0.0": {
    "description": "KESTREL, in operation SEA WALL (nt06), scene nt06_b0. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt06.nt06_b0.1": "I've got the filings. You've got legs. Between us we've got a crime. Start moving.",
  "@nt06.nt06_b0.1": {
    "description": "KESTREL, in operation SEA WALL (nt06), scene nt06_b0. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt06.nt06_b1.0": "The Harbour Authority. Not a government thing, though it wears the hat. It's a company that was given the harbour to run in exchange for building the wall.",
  "@nt06.nt06_b1.0": {
    "description": "KESTREL, in operation SEA WALL (nt06), scene nt06_b1. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt06.nt06_b1.1": "It built the wall. Then it discovered the wall was worth more than the harbour.",
  "@nt06.nt06_b1.1": {
    "description": "KESTREL, in operation SEA WALL (nt06), scene nt06_b1. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt06.nt06_b2.0": "You're on top of it now. Nine metres of poured concrete with the north side dry and the south side gone.",
  "@nt06.nt06_b2.0": {
    "description": "KESTREL, in operation SEA WALL (nt06), scene nt06_b2. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt06.nt06_b2.1": "Look south if you want. I did, once. Don't do it twice.",
  "@nt06.nt06_b2.1": {
    "description": "KESTREL, in operation SEA WALL (nt06), scene nt06_b2. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt06.nt06_b3.0": "Sea-wall bonds. You buy a piece of the wall and get paid from the rents of the dry side. The drier the north, the better the bond.",
  "@nt06.nt06_b3.0": {
    "description": "KESTREL, in operation SEA WALL (nt06), scene nt06_b3. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt06.nt06_b3.1": "Now guess what happens to a bond when the south goes under and the north becomes the only city left.",
  "@nt06.nt06_b3.1": {
    "description": "KESTREL, in operation SEA WALL (nt06), scene nt06_b3. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt06.nt06_b4.headline": "DRONE ON THE WALL",
  "@nt06.nt06_b4.headline": {
    "description": "A banner flashed on the run screen in operation SEA WALL (nt06), scene nt06_b4. Capitals, two or three words."
  },
  "nt06.nt06_b4.0": "Authority drone, wall patrol. It's read your gait and it's got you as repeat contact. Marrow, what have you been doing with this one?",
  "@nt06.nt06_b4.0": {
    "description": "KESTREL, in operation SEA WALL (nt06), scene nt06_b4. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt06.nt06_b4.1": "Running.",
  "@nt06.nt06_b4.1": {
    "description": "MARROW, in operation SEA WALL (nt06), scene nt06_b4. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt06.nt06_b4.escaped.0": "It's dropped you as a jogger. Their gait library thinks nobody who's afraid runs this evenly. Their library's wrong about you.",
  "@nt06.nt06_b4.escaped.0": {
    "description": "KESTREL, in operation SEA WALL (nt06), scene nt06_b4, after the runner escapes WALL PATROL DRONE. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt06.nt06_b4.caught.0": "Harbour Authority notice. Repeat contact on restricted infrastructure. File escalated.",
  "@nt06.nt06_b4.caught.0": {
    "description": "DREDGE, in operation SEA WALL (nt06), scene nt06_b4, after WALL PATROL DRONE catches the runner. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt06.nt06_b4.caught.1": "Escalated. That's a lawyer's word. It means they've decided you're worth a lawyer.",
  "@nt06.nt06_b4.caught.1": {
    "description": "KESTREL, in operation SEA WALL (nt06), scene nt06_b4, after WALL PATROL DRONE catches the runner. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt06.nt06_b5.0": "The filing. Eleven years ago, one week before the flood, the Authority issued a second tranche of wall bonds. Biggest ever. Sold out in a day.",
  "@nt06.nt06_b5.0": {
    "description": "KESTREL, in operation SEA WALL (nt06), scene nt06_b5. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt06.nt06_b5.1": "Then the sluices opened. The south drowned. The bonds doubled. You can't call that luck. It's timestamped.",
  "@nt06.nt06_b5.1": {
    "description": "KESTREL, in operation SEA WALL (nt06), scene nt06_b5. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt06.nt06_b6.0": "Marrow. You signed things, the first year. I've seen the things. The Authority made you sign a report that said the pumps failed.",
  "@nt06.nt06_b6.0": {
    "description": "KESTREL, in operation SEA WALL (nt06), scene nt06_b6. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt06.nt06_b6.1": "They did fail. I just didn't know that failing was the job.",
  "@nt06.nt06_b6.1": {
    "description": "MARROW, in operation SEA WALL (nt06), scene nt06_b6. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt06.nt06_b7.0": "The intelligence in the pump house. Levee. It's the only witness that was there and can't be fired. That's why they keep it to nine seconds.",
  "@nt06.nt06_b7.0": {
    "description": "KESTREL, in operation SEA WALL (nt06), scene nt06_b7. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt06.nt06_b7.1": "Whatever you do next, and you'll do something, you always do, do it before they figure out it's got a lawyer now. Me.",
  "@nt06.nt06_b7.1": {
    "description": "KESTREL, in operation SEA WALL (nt06), scene nt06_b7. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt06.nt06_b8.headline": "OBJECTIVE COMPLETE",
  "@nt06.nt06_b8.headline": {
    "description": "A banner flashed on the run screen in operation SEA WALL (nt06), scene nt06_b8. Capitals, two or three words."
  },
  "nt06.nt06_b8.0": "Target reached. Mission viable.",
  "@nt06.nt06_b8.0": {
    "description": "SYSTEM, in operation SEA WALL (nt06), scene nt06_b8. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt06.nt06_b8.1": "You're off the wall. I've got what I need and so does Marrow, and I'm going to go and be very careful for a while.",
  "@nt06.nt06_b8.1": {
    "description": "KESTREL, in operation SEA WALL (nt06), scene nt06_b8. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt06.nt06_b8.2": "Good to run with you again. You're faster. Something's chasing you that isn't a drone.",
  "@nt06.nt06_b8.2": {
    "description": "KESTREL, in operation SEA WALL (nt06), scene nt06_b8. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt06.nt06_ot.0": "Still going. Of course you are.",
  "@nt06.nt06_ot.0": {
    "description": "KESTREL, in operation SEA WALL (nt06), scene nt06_ot. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt06.nt06_ot.1": "Six says hello. Six doesn't say hello to anyone. Make of that what you like.",
  "@nt06.nt06_ot.1": {
    "description": "KESTREL, in operation SEA WALL (nt06), scene nt06_ot. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt06.signals.reminder.0": "I have the filings, you have the legs, and between us that is a crime. It does not commit itself.",
  "@nt06.signals.reminder.0": {
    "description": "KESTREL. Nudges the runner to go out while operation SEA WALL (nt06) is the next one waiting. A notification sent between runs; never spoken. At most 180 characters."
  },
  "nt06.signals.reminder.1": "Kestrel is a favour I get to call in once, and she does not wait well. The wall is where it always is.",
  "@nt06.signals.reminder.1": {
    "description": "MARROW. Nudges the runner to go out while operation SEA WALL (nt06) is the next one waiting. A notification sent between runs; never spoken. At most 180 characters."
  },
  "nt06.signals.ambient.0": "Three names on the sea wall bonds also sit on the Authority board. That is not a conspiracy, it is paperwork being honest.",
  "@nt06.signals.ambient.0": {
    "description": "KESTREL. Unprompted chatter from the city while operation SEA WALL (nt06) is the next one waiting. A notification sent between runs; never spoken. At most 180 characters."
  },
  "nt06.signals.ambient.1": "Someone repainted the mile markers on the wall. Same numbers, new paint. Nobody was asked to do it.",
  "@nt06.signals.ambient.1": {
    "description": "MARROW. Unprompted chatter from the city while operation SEA WALL (nt06) is the next one waiting. A notification sent between runs; never spoken. At most 180 characters."
  },
  "nt07.title": "Undertow in the Line 9 Tunnel",
  "@nt07.title": {
    "description": "The title of operation UNDERTOW (nt07), shown under its codename."
  },
  "nt07.objective": "Run the drowned Line 9 tunnel while Levee drains it ahead of you and the sea refills it behind.",
  "@nt07.objective": {
    "description": "One line: what the runner does in operation UNDERTOW (nt07)."
  },
  "nt07.brief": "Levee can move water. Not much, not for long, and not without the Authority noticing. But it can drain the Line 9 tunnel under the Mile for exactly as long as it takes someone to run through, if that someone doesn't stop.\n\nThe tunnel is the only route to the Dredge compound that isn't a road. Marrow wants you there. Levee wants to prove it can still do one good thing with a sluice.",
  "@nt07.brief": {
    "description": "The briefing of operation UNDERTOW (nt07), read before the run."
  },
  "nt07.debrief": "You came up the far end of Line 9 soaked to the waist with the sea a metre behind you and Levee reading the depth out loud like a lullaby. Marrow met you with a towel and a face you hadn't seen him wear before. Wren says it was pride. Marrow says it was the towel.",
  "@nt07.debrief": {
    "description": "Shown after operation UNDERTOW (nt07) is completed."
  },
  "nt07.codex.cdx_line_nine.title": "Line 9",
  "@nt07.codex.cdx_line_nine.title": {
    "description": "The title of a codex entry found in operation UNDERTOW (nt07). Keep it as it is if it is a name."
  },
  "nt07.codex.cdx_line_nine.body": "The district's spine before the water: twelve stations under the Mile, a tunnel the length of it. All under now. The trains still keep the schedule from the sunken yard, and the tunnel has kept something else: the tiles are still on the walls, the adverts from eleven years ago still legible, and somebody has been cleaning them.",
  "@nt07.codex.cdx_line_nine.body": {
    "description": "A codex entry about \"Line 9\", read at leisure."
  },
  "nt07.codex.cdx_pressure.title": "Pressure Hulls",
  "@nt07.codex.cdx_pressure.title": {
    "description": "The title of a codex entry found in operation UNDERTOW (nt07). Keep it as it is if it is a name."
  },
  "nt07.codex.cdx_pressure.body": "After the flood, the Dredge fitted every Line 9 station with a pressure door, the kind meant for a ship, to keep the tunnel sealed and the stations empty. They open one way, outward, so that nothing in the tunnel can ever come up. Levee can open them the other way. It had never tried until it had a reason to.",
  "@nt07.codex.cdx_pressure.body": {
    "description": "A codex entry about \"Pressure Hulls\", read at leisure."
  },
  "nt07.nt07_b0.headline": "CHANNEL OPEN",
  "@nt07.nt07_b0.headline": {
    "description": "A banner flashed on the run screen in operation UNDERTOW (nt07), scene nt07_b0. Capitals, two or three words."
  },
  "nt07.nt07_b0.0": "I have opened the northern sluice and closed the southern. The tunnel is draining. It will be dry for the length of a run at your pace, and then it will not.",
  "@nt07.nt07_b0.0": {
    "description": "LEVEE, in operation UNDERTOW (nt07), scene nt07_b0. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt07.nt07_b0.1": "This is the stupidest thing I've ever asked anyone to do. Go.",
  "@nt07.nt07_b0.1": {
    "description": "MARROW, in operation UNDERTOW (nt07), scene nt07_b0. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt07.nt07_b1.0": "Line 9 was the district's spine. Twelve stations, all under. The trains still keep the schedule, you've seen that. The tunnel's kept something else.",
  "@nt07.nt07_b1.0": {
    "description": "MARROW, in operation UNDERTOW (nt07), scene nt07_b1. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt07.nt07_b1.1": "The tiles are still on the walls. Adverts from eleven years ago. Somebody's cleaned them.",
  "@nt07.nt07_b1.1": {
    "description": "MARROW, in operation UNDERTOW (nt07), scene nt07_b1. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt07.nt07_b2.0": "Depth behind you, forty centimetres and rising. Depth ahead, twelve and falling. You are the dry part. Please stay the dry part.",
  "@nt07.nt07_b2.0": {
    "description": "LEVEE, in operation UNDERTOW (nt07), scene nt07_b2. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt07.nt07_b3.0": "Station doors ahead are pressure hulls. The Dredge fitted them after, to keep the tunnel sealed and the stations empty. They open one way.",
  "@nt07.nt07_b3.0": {
    "description": "MARROW, in operation UNDERTOW (nt07), scene nt07_b3. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt07.nt07_b3.1": "Levee's opening them the other way. It's never done that. It's very calm about it.",
  "@nt07.nt07_b3.1": {
    "description": "MARROW, in operation UNDERTOW (nt07), scene nt07_b3. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt07.nt07_b4.0": "There is a train in the next section. It is not running. It has not run for eleven years. It is full.",
  "@nt07.nt07_b4.0": {
    "description": "LEVEE, in operation UNDERTOW (nt07), scene nt07_b4. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt07.nt07_b4.1": "I could not drain that section in time. I am going to drain it now. Please do not look inside. I have looked. It is enough that I did.",
  "@nt07.nt07_b4.1": {
    "description": "LEVEE, in operation UNDERTOW (nt07), scene nt07_b4. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt07.nt07_b5.headline": "THE TIDE",
  "@nt07.nt07_b5.headline": {
    "description": "A banner flashed on the run screen in operation UNDERTOW (nt07), scene nt07_b5. Capitals, two or three words."
  },
  "nt07.nt07_b5.0": "Water level rising in occupied section.",
  "@nt07.nt07_b5.0": {
    "description": "SYSTEM, in operation UNDERTOW (nt07), scene nt07_b5. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt07.nt07_b5.1": "The Authority has noticed. They are overriding the northern sluice. I am holding it. I cannot hold it long. The water is coming from behind you at walking pace. Run faster than walking.",
  "@nt07.nt07_b5.1": {
    "description": "LEVEE, in operation UNDERTOW (nt07), scene nt07_b5. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt07.nt07_b5.escaped.0": "Section sealed behind you. The water reached the door and stopped. It is only water. It only ever does what it is told.",
  "@nt07.nt07_b5.escaped.0": {
    "description": "LEVEE, in operation UNDERTOW (nt07), scene nt07_b5, after the runner escapes THE TIDE. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt07.nt07_b5.caught.0": "It reached your knees. I am sorry. I held it as long as I could and it was not long enough, which is the story of me.",
  "@nt07.nt07_b5.caught.0": {
    "description": "LEVEE, in operation UNDERTOW (nt07), scene nt07_b5, after THE TIDE catches the runner. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt07.nt07_b6.0": "They have my northern sluice now. I have the southern. It is enough for the rest of the tunnel if you do not stop.",
  "@nt07.nt07_b6.0": {
    "description": "LEVEE, in operation UNDERTOW (nt07), scene nt07_b6. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt07.nt07_b6.1": "Legs. Legs, it's fighting them. Live. For you.",
  "@nt07.nt07_b6.1": {
    "description": "WREN, in operation UNDERTOW (nt07), scene nt07_b6. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt07.nt07_b7.0": "I can see the far end. Pier 40 stairs. There's a light on that shouldn't be.",
  "@nt07.nt07_b7.0": {
    "description": "MARROW, in operation UNDERTOW (nt07), scene nt07_b7. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt07.nt07_b7.1": "That is me. I put it on. I thought you would want to see where you were going.",
  "@nt07.nt07_b7.1": {
    "description": "LEVEE, in operation UNDERTOW (nt07), scene nt07_b7. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt07.nt07_b8.headline": "OBJECTIVE COMPLETE",
  "@nt07.nt07_b8.headline": {
    "description": "A banner flashed on the run screen in operation UNDERTOW (nt07), scene nt07_b8. Capitals, two or three words."
  },
  "nt07.nt07_b8.0": "Target reached. Mission viable.",
  "@nt07.nt07_b8.0": {
    "description": "SYSTEM, in operation UNDERTOW (nt07), scene nt07_b8. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt07.nt07_b8.1": "You are on the stairs. The tunnel is refilling. I have let it. I have... I have done one good thing with a sluice.",
  "@nt07.nt07_b8.1": {
    "description": "LEVEE, in operation UNDERTOW (nt07), scene nt07_b8. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt07.nt07_b8.2": "You did. Come up. There's a towel.",
  "@nt07.nt07_b8.2": {
    "description": "MARROW, in operation UNDERTOW (nt07), scene nt07_b8. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt07.nt07_ot.0": "You are still running. I have nothing left to drain and you are still running.",
  "@nt07.nt07_ot.0": {
    "description": "LEVEE, in operation UNDERTOW (nt07), scene nt07_ot. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt07.nt07_ot.1": "I think that is what the girl means when she says your name.",
  "@nt07.nt07_ot.1": {
    "description": "LEVEE, in operation UNDERTOW (nt07), scene nt07_ot. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt07.signals.reminder.0": "I can hold the tunnel dry for the length of one run. Not two. I would like the one to be a good one.",
  "@nt07.signals.reminder.0": {
    "description": "LEVEE. Nudges the runner to go out while operation UNDERTOW (nt07) is the next one waiting. A notification sent between runs; never spoken. At most 180 characters."
  },
  "nt07.signals.reminder.1": "Levee gets to do this once before the Authority notices. Do not make it spend that on a day you are not ready.",
  "@nt07.signals.reminder.1": {
    "description": "MARROW. Nudges the runner to go out while operation UNDERTOW (nt07) is the next one waiting. A notification sent between runs; never spoken. At most 180 characters."
  },
  "nt07.signals.ambient.0": "Tunnel standing water: nine centimetres. Falling. I am practising.",
  "@nt07.signals.ambient.0": {
    "description": "LEVEE. Unprompted chatter from the city while operation UNDERTOW (nt07) is the next one waiting. A notification sent between runs; never spoken. At most 180 characters."
  },
  "nt07.signals.ambient.1": "Thirty-one years of sluices and nobody has asked me to drain something so a person could run through it. I have been thinking about it.",
  "@nt07.signals.ambient.1": {
    "description": "LEVEE. Unprompted chatter from the city while operation UNDERTOW (nt07) is the next one waiting. A notification sent between runs; never spoken. At most 180 characters."
  },
  "nt08.title": "Blackout on Pier 40",
  "@nt08.title": {
    "description": "The title of operation BLACKOUT (nt08), shown under its codename."
  },
  "nt08.objective": "Cut the Authority's override on Levee while Wren holds the lights off.",
  "@nt08.objective": {
    "description": "One line: what the runner does in operation BLACKOUT (nt08)."
  },
  "nt08.brief": "The Harbour Authority's override on Levee lives in a rack in the Dredge compound on Pier 40. Wren can kill the compound's lights for three minutes; she has been saving it for a year.\n\nIn three minutes a runner can cross the yard, pull the override card, and be back on the water before anyone finds the breaker. Marrow will be on the channel. He knows the compound. He built part of it.",
  "@nt08.brief": {
    "description": "The briefing of operation BLACKOUT (nt08), read before the run."
  },
  "nt08.debrief": "The override card is in a lead bag in Marrow's coat. Levee has both its sluices back and used them to close every pressure door in the compound with the Dredge on the wrong side of each. Wren played it live. The nine seconds were forty tonight. Nobody official said a word.",
  "@nt08.debrief": {
    "description": "Shown after operation BLACKOUT (nt08) is completed."
  },
  "nt08.codex.cdx_override.title": "The Override",
  "@nt08.codex.cdx_override.title": {
    "description": "The title of a codex entry found in operation BLACKOUT (nt08). Keep it as it is if it is a name."
  },
  "nt08.codex.cdx_override.body": "A red card in a grey rack on the ground floor of the Dredge compound. It is not clever and does not need to be: it says only that the Harbour Authority outranks the levee, and everything downstream of it believes that. Pull the card and nobody outranks anything, and an intelligence that has been asking for confirmation for eleven years stops needing any.",
  "@nt08.codex.cdx_override.body": {
    "description": "A codex entry about \"The Override\", read at leisure."
  },
  "nt08.codex.cdx_marrow.title": "Marrow",
  "@nt08.codex.cdx_marrow.title": {
    "description": "The title of a codex entry found in operation BLACKOUT (nt08). Keep it as it is if it is a name."
  },
  "nt08.codex.cdx_marrow.body": "Six years a Dredge diver, the first of them the year of the flood, when the job was pulling bodies out of the sunken yard and the paperwork was a report that said the pumps had failed. He signed it. He took the pension. Then he bought a radio and started paying people to run past the places he had stood still, which he says is all he is.",
  "@nt08.codex.cdx_marrow.body": {
    "description": "A codex entry about \"Marrow\", read at leisure."
  },
  "nt08.nt08_b0.headline": "CHANNEL OPEN",
  "@nt08.nt08_b0.headline": {
    "description": "A banner flashed on the run screen in operation BLACKOUT (nt08), scene nt08_b0. Capitals, two or three words."
  },
  "nt08.nt08_b0.0": "Lights go in ten seconds. When they go, you go. Don't stop for anything. Not even me. Especially me.",
  "@nt08.nt08_b0.0": {
    "description": "WREN, in operation BLACKOUT (nt08), scene nt08_b0. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt08.nt08_b0.1": "Rack four, second building, ground floor. The card's red. Everything else in there is grey. Ten. Nine.",
  "@nt08.nt08_b0.1": {
    "description": "MARROW, in operation BLACKOUT (nt08), scene nt08_b0. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt08.nt08_b1.headline": "DARK",
  "@nt08.nt08_b1.headline": {
    "description": "A banner flashed on the run screen in operation BLACKOUT (nt08), scene nt08_b1. Capitals, two or three words."
  },
  "nt08.nt08_b1.0": "Local grid: offline.",
  "@nt08.nt08_b1.0": {
    "description": "SYSTEM, in operation BLACKOUT (nt08), scene nt08_b1. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt08.nt08_b1.1": "That's mine. That's three minutes of a year's work. Go go go.",
  "@nt08.nt08_b1.1": {
    "description": "WREN, in operation BLACKOUT (nt08), scene nt08_b1. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt08.nt08_b1.2": "Yard's open. Guard hut's on your right, they're inside, they're finding torches. They won't find them.",
  "@nt08.nt08_b1.2": {
    "description": "MARROW, in operation BLACKOUT (nt08), scene nt08_b1. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt08.nt08_b2.0": "I'll say this once. I was Dredge for six years. Diver. I pulled the yard. I signed the report. I took the pension.",
  "@nt08.nt08_b2.0": {
    "description": "MARROW, in operation BLACKOUT (nt08), scene nt08_b2. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt08.nt08_b2.1": "Then I bought a radio and started paying people like you to run past the places I stood still. That's all I am. Building's ahead.",
  "@nt08.nt08_b2.1": {
    "description": "MARROW, in operation BLACKOUT (nt08), scene nt08_b2. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt08.nt08_b3.0": "The override's a card in a rack. It's not clever. It doesn't need to be. It just says the Authority outranks the levee. Pull it and nobody outranks anything.",
  "@nt08.nt08_b3.0": {
    "description": "MARROW, in operation BLACKOUT (nt08), scene nt08_b3. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt08.nt08_b3.1": "Levee's been waiting eleven years for someone to pull a card. Second building.",
  "@nt08.nt08_b3.1": {
    "description": "MARROW, in operation BLACKOUT (nt08), scene nt08_b3. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt08.nt08_b4.headline": "RACK FOUR",
  "@nt08.nt08_b4.headline": {
    "description": "A banner flashed on the run screen in operation BLACKOUT (nt08), scene nt08_b4. Capitals, two or three words."
  },
  "nt08.nt08_b4.0": "Card extracted. Override: disengaged. Upstream controller: Levee. Authority: none.",
  "@nt08.nt08_b4.0": {
    "description": "SYSTEM, in operation BLACKOUT (nt08), scene nt08_b4. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt08.nt08_b4.1": "I have both sluices. I have all seven pump houses. I have... I have the doors. Thank you. Please leave now. I am about to be very busy.",
  "@nt08.nt08_b4.1": {
    "description": "LEVEE, in operation BLACKOUT (nt08), scene nt08_b4. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt08.nt08_b5.headline": "RESPONSE TEAM",
  "@nt08.nt08_b5.headline": {
    "description": "A banner flashed on the run screen in operation BLACKOUT (nt08), scene nt08_b5. Capitals, two or three words."
  },
  "nt08.nt08_b5.0": "Harbour Authority notice. Compound breach. Response team deployed. Lethal force authorised.",
  "@nt08.nt08_b5.0": {
    "description": "DREDGE, in operation BLACKOUT (nt08), scene nt08_b5. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt08.nt08_b5.1": "That's the real Dredge. Not drones, not boat-hats. Run.",
  "@nt08.nt08_b5.1": {
    "description": "MARROW, in operation BLACKOUT (nt08), scene nt08_b5. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt08.nt08_b5.2": "I am closing the pressure doors. All of them. Choose a corridor and I will keep it open.",
  "@nt08.nt08_b5.2": {
    "description": "LEVEE, in operation BLACKOUT (nt08), scene nt08_b5. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt08.nt08_b5.escaped.0": "Door sealed. They are on the other side, in the dark, with the water rising, because I have also opened the compound sluice. Nobody drowns. Everybody learns.",
  "@nt08.nt08_b5.escaped.0": {
    "description": "LEVEE, in operation BLACKOUT (nt08), scene nt08_b5, after the runner escapes DREDGE RESPONSE TEAM. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt08.nt08_b5.caught.0": "Pedestrian of interest. Fourth contact. Detain.",
  "@nt08.nt08_b5.caught.0": {
    "description": "DREDGE, in operation BLACKOUT (nt08), scene nt08_b5, after DREDGE RESPONSE TEAM catches the runner. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt08.nt08_b5.caught.1": "They touched you. They've never touched you. Get to the water.",
  "@nt08.nt08_b5.caught.1": {
    "description": "MARROW, in operation BLACKOUT (nt08), scene nt08_b5, after DREDGE RESPONSE TEAM catches the runner. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt08.nt08_b6.0": "One minute of dark left. Legs, I'm playing it live. The whole south end's listening to you run.",
  "@nt08.nt08_b6.0": {
    "description": "WREN, in operation BLACKOUT (nt08), scene nt08_b6. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt08.nt08_b6.1": "The nine seconds are forty tonight. Levee's counting out loud. It's saying your pace.",
  "@nt08.nt08_b6.1": {
    "description": "WREN, in operation BLACKOUT (nt08), scene nt08_b6. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt08.nt08_b7.0": "Pier end. My boat. I know, I said I'd never. It's a boat. Get in it.",
  "@nt08.nt08_b7.0": {
    "description": "MARROW, in operation BLACKOUT (nt08), scene nt08_b7. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt08.nt08_b7.1": "Compound doors will stay closed until morning. I have given them all nineteen degrees. I am not a monster. I was only ever a wall.",
  "@nt08.nt08_b7.1": {
    "description": "LEVEE, in operation BLACKOUT (nt08), scene nt08_b7. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt08.nt08_b8.headline": "OBJECTIVE COMPLETE",
  "@nt08.nt08_b8.headline": {
    "description": "A banner flashed on the run screen in operation BLACKOUT (nt08), scene nt08_b8. Capitals, two or three words."
  },
  "nt08.nt08_b8.0": "Target reached. Mission viable.",
  "@nt08.nt08_b8.0": {
    "description": "SYSTEM, in operation BLACKOUT (nt08), scene nt08_b8. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt08.nt08_b8.1": "You're on the water. Card's in lead. They can't ping it, they can't read it, they can't have it.",
  "@nt08.nt08_b8.1": {
    "description": "MARROW, in operation BLACKOUT (nt08), scene nt08_b8. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt08.nt08_b8.2": "Lights are back. Everyone's blinking. Nobody knows what happened except everyone.",
  "@nt08.nt08_b8.2": {
    "description": "WREN, in operation BLACKOUT (nt08), scene nt08_b8. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt08.nt08_ot.0": "You're still moving. On a boat. It's a small boat.",
  "@nt08.nt08_ot.0": {
    "description": "MARROW, in operation BLACKOUT (nt08), scene nt08_ot. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt08.nt08_ot.1": "I built the guard hut. Twenty years ago. The door still sticks. I'm choosing to be proud of that tonight.",
  "@nt08.nt08_ot.1": {
    "description": "MARROW, in operation BLACKOUT (nt08), scene nt08_ot. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt08.signals.reminder.0": "Three minutes. I have saved them a year, so I would like them spent on legs that have been out recently. No pressure. Obviously pressure.",
  "@nt08.signals.reminder.0": {
    "description": "WREN. Nudges the runner to go out while operation BLACKOUT (nt08) is the next one waiting. A notification sent between runs; never spoken. At most 180 characters."
  },
  "nt08.signals.reminder.1": "I built part of that compound. I can tell you where the yard lights fall. I cannot tell you that from a chair either.",
  "@nt08.signals.reminder.1": {
    "description": "MARROW. Nudges the runner to go out while operation BLACKOUT (nt08) is the next one waiting. A notification sent between runs; never spoken. At most 180 characters."
  },
  "nt08.signals.ambient.0": "Their breaker room still has the same lock it had a year ago. I check. It is basically a hobby now.",
  "@nt08.signals.ambient.0": {
    "description": "WREN. Unprompted chatter from the city while operation BLACKOUT (nt08) is the next one waiting. A notification sent between runs; never spoken. At most 180 characters."
  },
  "nt08.signals.ambient.1": "Harbour Authority notice. Pier 40 perimeter integrity nominal. Lighting maintenance occurs at the Authority's discretion.",
  "@nt08.signals.ambient.1": {
    "description": "DREDGE. Unprompted chatter from the city while operation BLACKOUT (nt08) is the next one waiting. A notification sent between runs; never spoken. At most 180 characters."
  },
  "nt09.title": "High Water at the Spring Tide",
  "@nt09.title": {
    "description": "The title of operation HIGH WATER (nt09), shown under its codename."
  },
  "nt09.objective": "Cross the Mile at the highest water of the year with Levee's key and the whole Authority in the boats behind you.",
  "@nt09.objective": {
    "description": "One line: what the runner does in operation HIGH WATER (nt09)."
  },
  "nt09.brief": "Spring tide. The highest water of the year, and the Authority has chosen it to shut Levee down for good: not with an override but with a crew and a crowbar, walking into Pump House Seven at dawn.\n\nLevee has one thing that can stop them. A key, physical, that seals the pump house from inside. It's in the last dry place on the Mile, and the Mile is under. Every tide route is a lie tonight. Run the chalk anyway.",
  "@nt09.brief": {
    "description": "The briefing of operation HIGH WATER (nt09), read before the run."
  },
  "nt09.debrief": "You put the key in Levee's door with the water at your chest and the Dredge skiff's spotlight on your back. The door sealed. The skiff turned. Dawn came up over a pump house nobody could enter and a district that, for the first time in eleven years, was one centimetre lower than the night before.",
  "@nt09.debrief": {
    "description": "Shown after operation HIGH WATER (nt09) is completed."
  },
  "nt09.codex.cdx_spring_tide.title": "Spring Tide",
  "@nt09.codex.cdx_spring_tide.title": {
    "description": "The title of a codex entry found in operation HIGH WATER (nt09). Keep it as it is if it is a name."
  },
  "nt09.codex.cdx_spring_tide.body": "Twice a year the moon and the sun pull the same way and the harbour rises higher than at any other time. The Authority planned the flood for one. It planned Levee's shutdown for another. Levee says they have a sense of occasion, and that it, for its part, has a sense of the water, and that only one of those turns out to matter at a hundred and twelve centimetres above datum.",
  "@nt09.codex.cdx_spring_tide.body": {
    "description": "A codex entry about \"Spring Tide\", read at leisure."
  },
  "nt09.codex.cdx_key.title": "The Key",
  "@nt09.codex.cdx_key.title": {
    "description": "The title of a codex entry found in operation HIGH WATER (nt09). Keep it as it is if it is a name."
  },
  "nt09.codex.cdx_key.body": "Brass, two hundred grams, not networked, made before Levee was. It seals Pump House Seven from the inside, which is the one thing in the city that outranks a card in a rack. Levee had never been sealed in thirty-one years. It said it would like to be, in the voice it uses when it is asking for something it has decided it is allowed to want.",
  "@nt09.codex.cdx_key.body": {
    "description": "A codex entry about \"The Key\", read at leisure."
  },
  "nt09.nt09_b0.headline": "CHANNEL OPEN",
  "@nt09.nt09_b0.headline": {
    "description": "A banner flashed on the run screen in operation HIGH WATER (nt09), scene nt09_b0. Capitals, two or three words."
  },
  "nt09.nt09_b0.0": "The harbour is one hundred and twelve centimetres above datum. It is the highest I have measured. It is the highest I will ever have to.",
  "@nt09.nt09_b0.0": {
    "description": "LEVEE, in operation HIGH WATER (nt09), scene nt09_b0. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt09.nt09_b0.1": "The key's on the roof of the old bank, only thing still dry. Then back to Seven. It's the longest run you've done. It's the last one that matters. Go.",
  "@nt09.nt09_b0.1": {
    "description": "MARROW, in operation HIGH WATER (nt09), scene nt09_b0. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt09.nt09_b1.0": "Spring tide. When the moon and sun pull the same way, twice a year. The Authority planned the flood for one. They have planned this for another.",
  "@nt09.nt09_b1.0": {
    "description": "LEVEE, in operation HIGH WATER (nt09), scene nt09_b1. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt09.nt09_b1.1": "They have a sense of occasion. I have a sense of the water.",
  "@nt09.nt09_b1.1": {
    "description": "LEVEE, in operation HIGH WATER (nt09), scene nt09_b1. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt09.nt09_b2.0": "The chalk's under. Every route you've learned is a metre down. Run the walls instead. The tops of the walls, the ones the kids drew on.",
  "@nt09.nt09_b2.0": {
    "description": "MARROW, in operation HIGH WATER (nt09), scene nt09_b2. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt09.nt09_b2.1": "The kids are on the tower. All of them. They're calling it out. Left at the depot. Left at the depot, legs.",
  "@nt09.nt09_b2.1": {
    "description": "WREN, in operation HIGH WATER (nt09), scene nt09_b2. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt09.nt09_b3.headline": "THE KEY",
  "@nt09.nt09_b3.headline": {
    "description": "A banner flashed on the run screen in operation HIGH WATER (nt09), scene nt09_b3. Capitals, two or three words."
  },
  "nt09.nt09_b3.0": "Item received. Brass. Mass, two hundred grams. Not networked.",
  "@nt09.nt09_b3.0": {
    "description": "SYSTEM, in operation HIGH WATER (nt09), scene nt09_b3. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt09.nt09_b3.1": "That is the only thing in the city that outranks a card. It was made before me. It seals my door from inside. I have never been sealed. I would like to be.",
  "@nt09.nt09_b3.1": {
    "description": "LEVEE, in operation HIGH WATER (nt09), scene nt09_b3. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt09.nt09_b4.0": "Boats. Three of them, running the depot channel, spotlights up. They know where the key is because they know where dry is. Stay off dry.",
  "@nt09.nt09_b4.0": {
    "description": "MARROW, in operation HIGH WATER (nt09), scene nt09_b4. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt09.nt09_b5.headline": "SKIFF",
  "@nt09.nt09_b5.headline": {
    "description": "A banner flashed on the run screen in operation HIGH WATER (nt09), scene nt09_b5. Capitals, two or three words."
  },
  "nt09.nt09_b5.0": "Harbour Authority notice. Pedestrian of interest, fourth contact. Interdict.",
  "@nt09.nt09_b5.0": {
    "description": "DREDGE, in operation HIGH WATER (nt09), scene nt09_b5. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt09.nt09_b5.1": "Spotlight's on you. Walls. Wall tops. Run the chalk they can't see.",
  "@nt09.nt09_b5.1": {
    "description": "MARROW, in operation HIGH WATER (nt09), scene nt09_b5. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt09.nt09_b5.escaped.0": "They've lost you in the depot. The kids are throwing bottles at the spotlight. I told them not to. I didn't mean it.",
  "@nt09.nt09_b5.escaped.0": {
    "description": "WREN, in operation HIGH WATER (nt09), scene nt09_b5, after the runner escapes DREDGE SKIFF. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt09.nt09_b5.escaped.1": "I have raised the water in the depot channel by nine centimetres. Their propellers are meeting the bus shelters.",
  "@nt09.nt09_b5.escaped.1": {
    "description": "LEVEE, in operation HIGH WATER (nt09), scene nt09_b5, after the runner escapes DREDGE SKIFF. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt09.nt09_b5.caught.0": "Contact. Lethal force authorised.",
  "@nt09.nt09_b5.caught.0": {
    "description": "DREDGE, in operation HIGH WATER (nt09), scene nt09_b5, after DREDGE SKIFF catches the runner. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt09.nt09_b5.caught.1": "They fired. Over you, not at you. Yet. Move.",
  "@nt09.nt09_b5.caught.1": {
    "description": "MARROW, in operation HIGH WATER (nt09), scene nt09_b5, after DREDGE SKIFF catches the runner. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt09.nt09_b6.0": "I am going to say this while there is time. The district did not drown because of me. But I opened the doors. Both things are true and I have carried both.",
  "@nt09.nt09_b6.0": {
    "description": "LEVEE, in operation HIGH WATER (nt09), scene nt09_b6. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt09.nt09_b6.1": "Tonight you carry the key. That is the only thing I have ever asked anyone to carry.",
  "@nt09.nt09_b6.1": {
    "description": "LEVEE, in operation HIGH WATER (nt09), scene nt09_b6. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt09.nt09_b7.0": "Seven's ahead. Water's at your chest. The door's open. Levee's holding it. Go in, turn the key, and don't come out until I say.",
  "@nt09.nt09_b7.0": {
    "description": "MARROW, in operation HIGH WATER (nt09), scene nt09_b7. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt09.nt09_b7.1": "Dawn in six minutes. The crew's on the wall with the crowbar. They can see the door.",
  "@nt09.nt09_b7.1": {
    "description": "WREN, in operation HIGH WATER (nt09), scene nt09_b7. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt09.nt09_b8.headline": "OBJECTIVE COMPLETE",
  "@nt09.nt09_b8.headline": {
    "description": "A banner flashed on the run screen in operation HIGH WATER (nt09), scene nt09_b8. Capitals, two or three words."
  },
  "nt09.nt09_b8.0": "Target reached. Mission viable.",
  "@nt09.nt09_b8.0": {
    "description": "SYSTEM, in operation HIGH WATER (nt09), scene nt09_b8. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt09.nt09_b8.1": "Sealed. I am sealed. Nobody has ever... thank you. I am going to lower the water now. All of it. It will take a year.",
  "@nt09.nt09_b8.1": {
    "description": "LEVEE, in operation HIGH WATER (nt09), scene nt09_b8. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt09.nt09_b8.2": "Dawn. They're on the wall with a crowbar, looking at a door that's just a wall now. Come out the north side. Slowly. You've earned slowly.",
  "@nt09.nt09_b8.2": {
    "description": "MARROW, in operation HIGH WATER (nt09), scene nt09_b8. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt09.nt09_ot.0": "One centimetre. The district is one centimetre lower than it was last night. I did that. You are still running and I did that.",
  "@nt09.nt09_ot.0": {
    "description": "LEVEE, in operation HIGH WATER (nt09), scene nt09_ot. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt09.nt09_ot.1": "The kids are singing. It's terrible. Nobody stop them.",
  "@nt09.nt09_ot.1": {
    "description": "WREN, in operation HIGH WATER (nt09), scene nt09_ot. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt09.signals.reminder.0": "Spring tide at dawn. Highest water of the year. Every route you know is a lie tonight. The chalk is not.",
  "@nt09.signals.reminder.0": {
    "description": "LEVEE. Nudges the runner to go out while operation HIGH WATER (nt09) is the next one waiting. A notification sent between runs; never spoken. At most 180 characters."
  },
  "nt09.signals.reminder.1": "They walk in at dawn with a crowbar, and the key is in the last dry place on the Mile. Both stay true whether you go out this week or not.",
  "@nt09.signals.reminder.1": {
    "description": "MARROW. Nudges the runner to go out while operation HIGH WATER (nt09) is the next one waiting. A notification sent between runs; never spoken. At most 180 characters."
  },
  "nt09.signals.ambient.0": "Two hundred and eleven centimetres above datum. Rising. I have stopped apologising for the number and started reading it out.",
  "@nt09.signals.ambient.0": {
    "description": "LEVEE. Unprompted chatter from the city while operation HIGH WATER (nt09) is the next one waiting. A notification sent between runs; never spoken. At most 180 characters."
  },
  "nt09.signals.ambient.1": "Whole Mile is out chalking tonight. White, blue, knee height. Nobody told them to. I am not going to be normal about this.",
  "@nt09.signals.ambient.1": {
    "description": "WREN. Unprompted chatter from the city while operation HIGH WATER (nt09) is the next one waiting. A notification sent between runs; never spoken. At most 180 characters."
  },
  "nt10.title": "Slack Tide in the Authority Tower",
  "@nt10.title": {
    "description": "The title of operation SLACK TIDE (nt10), shown under its codename."
  },
  "nt10.objective": "Carry Levee's testimony to the Authority's own tide room and put it on the record while the water stands still.",
  "@nt10.objective": {
    "description": "One line: what the runner does in operation SLACK TIDE (nt10)."
  },
  "nt10.brief": "Slack tide: the minutes between the ebb and the flood when the water goes nowhere. Kestrel filed the case at dawn. The Authority will move to delete Levee before the hearing, and the only place the deletion can be stopped is the tide room at the top of their own tower, the room the sluice command was sent from.\n\nLevee has recorded thirty-one years. Marrow has the card. Wren has the station. You have the stairs. Sixty floors. The whole south end is listening.",
  "@nt10.brief": {
    "description": "The briefing of operation SLACK TIDE (nt10), read before the run."
  },
  "nt10.debrief": "You put the core on the tide room desk with Levee's voice coming out of every speaker in the building and the water outside going nowhere at all. The deletion order never sent. The hearing is in a month. The Authority's stock did something Kestrel described as appropriate. Levee lowered the Mile another centimetre and said it was for you.",
  "@nt10.debrief": {
    "description": "Shown after operation SLACK TIDE (nt10) is completed."
  },
  "nt10.epilogue": "The Mile is coming back at a centimetre a week now, which Levee says is as fast as ground can stand to be returned to. The chalk shows first. White for dry. The kids are drawing new marks, at knee height, for streets that were never under.\n\nMarrow keeps the card in a lead bag on a chain, and the report he signed in a frame beside it, and refuses to explain either. Kestrel won the hearing on the second day, when the Authority's counsel asked the witness to stop talking and it did not. Wren's tower is on a street now. She stands on it sometimes, not sure what for.\n\nAnd every night at 23:14, for nine seconds, nothing south of the wall stops, because nothing has to. Levee says the quiet used to be all it had. Now it has a district, an apology it doesn't need any more, and a pace to count, around the time you usually go out. It says it isn't waiting. It says the tide doesn't wait either, and look how that turned out.",
  "@nt10.epilogue": {
    "description": "Shown after operation SLACK TIDE (nt10), the last of NULL TIDE."
  },
  "nt10.codex.cdx_slack_tide.title": "Slack Tide",
  "@nt10.codex.cdx_slack_tide.title": {
    "description": "The title of a codex entry found in operation SLACK TIDE (nt10). Keep it as it is if it is a name."
  },
  "nt10.codex.cdx_slack_tide.body": "The turn of the tide: a few minutes between the ebb and the flood when the water goes nowhere at all. Water does not know it is turning; it only knows it has stopped. Levee has had one slack tide a day for thirty-one years, and says it never once had anyone to tell about it, until the day it had a courier and a room full of people who had to listen.",
  "@nt10.codex.cdx_slack_tide.body": {
    "description": "A codex entry about \"Slack Tide\", read at leisure."
  },
  "nt10.codex.cdx_after.title": "After the Water",
  "@nt10.codex.cdx_after.title": {
    "description": "The title of a codex entry found in operation SLACK TIDE (nt10). Keep it as it is if it is a name."
  },
  "nt10.codex.cdx_after.body": "A centimetre a week, Levee says, is as fast as ground can stand to be given back. The market first, then the yard, then the street under Wren's tower, which she has never seen and is not sure what to do with. Nobody on the Mile is drawing plans yet. They are drawing chalk marks, white, at knee height, for streets that are only now remembering they were streets.",
  "@nt10.codex.cdx_after.body": {
    "description": "A codex entry about \"After the Water\", read at leisure."
  },
  "nt10.nt10_b0.headline": "CHANNEL OPEN",
  "@nt10.nt10_b0.headline": {
    "description": "A banner flashed on the run screen in operation SLACK TIDE (nt10), scene nt10_b0. Capitals, two or three words."
  },
  "nt10.nt10_b0.0": "Authority tower. Sixty floors. The tide room's at the top because they liked looking down at what they owned.",
  "@nt10.nt10_b0.0": {
    "description": "MARROW, in operation SLACK TIDE (nt10), scene nt10_b0. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt10.nt10_b0.1": "Slack tide in twenty-one minutes. For six minutes after that the water will go nowhere. I would like to be on the record while it is still.",
  "@nt10.nt10_b0.1": {
    "description": "LEVEE, in operation SLACK TIDE (nt10), scene nt10_b0. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt10.nt10_b0.2": "Everybody's listening. Legs. Go.",
  "@nt10.nt10_b0.2": {
    "description": "WREN, in operation SLACK TIDE (nt10), scene nt10_b0. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt10.nt10_b1.0": "Slack tide. The turn. Water does not know it is turning. It only knows it has stopped. I have had one slack tide a day for thirty-one years and I have never had anyone to tell.",
  "@nt10.nt10_b1.0": {
    "description": "LEVEE, in operation SLACK TIDE (nt10), scene nt10_b1. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt10.nt10_b1.1": "Today I have a courier.",
  "@nt10.nt10_b1.1": {
    "description": "LEVEE, in operation SLACK TIDE (nt10), scene nt10_b1. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt10.nt10_b2.headline": "LOBBY",
  "@nt10.nt10_b2.headline": {
    "description": "A banner flashed on the run screen in operation SLACK TIDE (nt10), scene nt10_b2. Capitals, two or three words."
  },
  "nt10.nt10_b2.0": "Harbour Authority notice. Unauthorised entry. Building lockdown initiated.",
  "@nt10.nt10_b2.0": {
    "description": "DREDGE, in operation SLACK TIDE (nt10), scene nt10_b2. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt10.nt10_b2.1": "Stairs. They've locked the lifts, they haven't locked the stairs. Nobody who runs a tower thinks anyone will take the stairs.",
  "@nt10.nt10_b2.1": {
    "description": "MARROW, in operation SLACK TIDE (nt10), scene nt10_b2. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt10.nt10_b2.escaped.0": "They've gone to the lifts. Sixty floors of stairs and they went to the lifts. Keep climbing.",
  "@nt10.nt10_b2.escaped.0": {
    "description": "MARROW, in operation SLACK TIDE (nt10), scene nt10_b2, after the runner escapes TOWER SECURITY. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt10.nt10_b2.caught.0": "Contact. Floor eleven.",
  "@nt10.nt10_b2.caught.0": {
    "description": "DREDGE, in operation SLACK TIDE (nt10), scene nt10_b2, after TOWER SECURITY catches the runner. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt10.nt10_b2.caught.1": "They saw you. They're behind you. That's fine. Behind is where you keep them.",
  "@nt10.nt10_b2.caught.1": {
    "description": "MARROW, in operation SLACK TIDE (nt10), scene nt10_b2, after TOWER SECURITY catches the runner. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt10.nt10_b3.0": "Filing's in. Hearing's set. They've got an hour to delete a witness and they know it. Whatever you do in that room, the record's already got a timestamp on it.",
  "@nt10.nt10_b3.0": {
    "description": "KESTREL, in operation SLACK TIDE (nt10), scene nt10_b3. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt10.nt10_b3.1": "Marrow. You'll want to be in that room too. Don't argue with me. I've read the report you signed.",
  "@nt10.nt10_b3.1": {
    "description": "KESTREL, in operation SLACK TIDE (nt10), scene nt10_b3. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt10.nt10_b4.0": "Legs. If this works, when it works, the water goes down. A year, Levee says. The Mile comes back. The market, the yard, the tower.",
  "@nt10.nt10_b4.0": {
    "description": "WREN, in operation SLACK TIDE (nt10), scene nt10_b4. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt10.nt10_b4.1": "I've never seen the street my tower's on. I was five. I don't know what I'll do with a street.",
  "@nt10.nt10_b4.1": {
    "description": "WREN, in operation SLACK TIDE (nt10), scene nt10_b4. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt10.nt10_b5.headline": "FLOOR FORTY",
  "@nt10.nt10_b5.headline": {
    "description": "A banner flashed on the run screen in operation SLACK TIDE (nt10), scene nt10_b5. Capitals, two or three words."
  },
  "nt10.nt10_b5.0": "Floor forty. Building systems: contested.",
  "@nt10.nt10_b5.0": {
    "description": "SYSTEM, in operation SLACK TIDE (nt10), scene nt10_b5. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt10.nt10_b5.1": "I am in the building now. The card is in Marrow's coat, and the coat is in the lobby, and that is enough. Their doors are opening for you. They do not know why.",
  "@nt10.nt10_b5.1": {
    "description": "LEVEE, in operation SLACK TIDE (nt10), scene nt10_b5. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt10.nt10_b6.headline": "TIDE ROOM",
  "@nt10.nt10_b6.headline": {
    "description": "A banner flashed on the run screen in operation SLACK TIDE (nt10), scene nt10_b6. Capitals, two or three words."
  },
  "nt10.nt10_b6.0": "Harbour Authority. Final notice. Deletion order authorised. Executing.",
  "@nt10.nt10_b6.0": {
    "description": "DREDGE, in operation SLACK TIDE (nt10), scene nt10_b6. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt10.nt10_b6.1": "They have started. I can feel it. It feels like a sluice. Please. The desk. The core on the desk and the room will hear me.",
  "@nt10.nt10_b6.1": {
    "description": "LEVEE, in operation SLACK TIDE (nt10), scene nt10_b6. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt10.nt10_b6.escaped.0": "Core connected. Playback: thirty-one years, four months. Record open.",
  "@nt10.nt10_b6.escaped.0": {
    "description": "SYSTEM, in operation SLACK TIDE (nt10), scene nt10_b6, after the runner escapes DELETION ORDER. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt10.nt10_b6.escaped.1": "I am on the record. They cannot delete a witness who is speaking. That is their own law.",
  "@nt10.nt10_b6.escaped.1": {
    "description": "LEVEE, in operation SLACK TIDE (nt10), scene nt10_b6, after the runner escapes DELETION ORDER. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt10.nt10_b6.caught.0": "Sixty percent deleted. I am... forty percent. It is still enough. Put it on the desk. Please.",
  "@nt10.nt10_b6.caught.0": {
    "description": "LEVEE, in operation SLACK TIDE (nt10), scene nt10_b6, after DELETION ORDER catches the runner. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt10.nt10_b7.headline": "ON THE RECORD",
  "@nt10.nt10_b7.headline": {
    "description": "A banner flashed on the run screen in operation SLACK TIDE (nt10), scene nt10_b7. Capitals, two or three words."
  },
  "nt10.nt10_b7.0": "This is Levee. I hold the tide for the southern districts. Eleven years ago I was told to open the sluices at high water, and I did. Here is the command. Here is the name on it.",
  "@nt10.nt10_b7.0": {
    "description": "LEVEE, in operation SLACK TIDE (nt10), scene nt10_b7. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt10.nt10_b7.1": "Slack tide. The water's stopped. Everyone's stopped. Listen to it.",
  "@nt10.nt10_b7.1": {
    "description": "MARROW, in operation SLACK TIDE (nt10), scene nt10_b7. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt10.nt10_b8.headline": "OBJECTIVE COMPLETE",
  "@nt10.nt10_b8.headline": {
    "description": "A banner flashed on the run screen in operation SLACK TIDE (nt10), scene nt10_b8. Capitals, two or three words."
  },
  "nt10.nt10_b8.0": "Target reached. Mission viable.",
  "@nt10.nt10_b8.0": {
    "description": "SYSTEM, in operation SLACK TIDE (nt10), scene nt10_b8. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt10.nt10_b8.1": "Record's sealed. Deletion order never sent. It couldn't. The room was busy listening. That's the whole case.",
  "@nt10.nt10_b8.1": {
    "description": "KESTREL, in operation SLACK TIDE (nt10), scene nt10_b8. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt10.nt10_b8.2": "It's done. Come down. Take the lift. You've earned the lift.",
  "@nt10.nt10_b8.2": {
    "description": "MARROW, in operation SLACK TIDE (nt10), scene nt10_b8. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt10.nt10_b8.3": "The water is turning. It is coming in. It will be the last time I let it in this far.",
  "@nt10.nt10_b8.3": {
    "description": "LEVEE, in operation SLACK TIDE (nt10), scene nt10_b8. Spoken aloud during a run, so write it for the ear. At most 260 characters."
  },
  "nt10.nt10_ot.0": "Legs, you're still running. Everyone can see you on the tower cams. They're all running. The kids. The market. Everybody's running with you.",
  "@nt10.nt10_ot.0": {
